window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-01-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1"]={"id":"CGL-01-OCT-2026-SHIFT-1","title":"CGL 01 OCT 2026 SHIFT 1","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072581","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Select the letter-cluster from among the given options that can replace the question mark (?) in the following series:<br>LZWT, LVOH, LRGV, LN YJ, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिए गए विकल्पों में से वह अक्षर-समूह चुनिए जो निम्नलिखित श्रेणी में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर आ सके:<br>LZWT, LVOH, LRGV, LNYJ, ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"LJQX"},"2":{"en":"LKJH"},"3":{"en":"LOIU"},"4":{"en":"LDFS"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letter L stays the same in every cluster<br>The second letters Z, V, R, N move four places back each time, so the next second letter is J<br>The third letters W, O, G, Y move eight places back each time, so the next third letter is Q<br>The fourth letters T, H, V, J move alternately twelve places back and fourteen places ahead: T&#8594;H, H&#8594;V, V&#8594;J, so after J the step is fourteen places ahead and gives X<br>Hence the next cluster is LJQX<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): LJQX.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक समूह में पहला अक्षर L वही रहता है<br>दूसरे अक्षर Z, V, R, N प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर J है<br>तीसरे अक्षर W, O, G, Y प्रत्येक बार आठ स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर Q है<br>चौथे अक्षर T, H, V, J बारी-बारी बारह स्थान पीछे तथा चौदह स्थान आगे जाते हैं: T&#8594;H, H&#8594;V, V&#8594;J, अतः J के बाद चौदह स्थान आगे का चरण X देता है<br>इसलिए अगला समूह LJQX है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): LJQX है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072582","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A person bought an article for Rs. 1200 and sold it at a loss of 10%. What is the selling price? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति ने 1200 रुपये में वस्तु खरीदी और उसे 10% हानि पर बेच दिया। विक्रय मूल्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rs. 1050","hi":"1050 रुपये"},"2":{"en":"Rs. 1090","hi":"1090 रुपये"},"3":{"en":"Rs. 1060","hi":"1060 रुपये"},"4":{"en":"Rs. 1080","hi":"1080 रुपये"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A loss of 10% means the selling price is 90% of the cost price<br>So the selling price is 1200 × 90 / 100 = 1080<br>Hence the selling price is Rs. 1080<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Rs. 1080.</b>","hi":"10% हानि का अर्थ है कि विक्रय मूल्य लागत मूल्य का 90% है<br>अतः विक्रय मूल्य 1200 × 90 / 100 = 1080 है<br>इसलिए विक्रय मूल्य 1080 रुपये है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 1080 रुपये है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072583","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the missing number: 43 : 129 :: 62 : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए: 43 : 129 :: 62 : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"142"},"2":{"en":"146"},"3":{"en":"145"},"4":{"en":"186"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The second number is three times the first number: 43 × 3 = 129 ✔<br>Applying the same relation, 62 × 3 = 186<br>Hence the missing number is 186<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 186.</b>","hi":"दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या की तीन गुनी है: 43 × 3 = 129 ✔<br>वही संबंध लगाने से 62 × 3 = 186<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 186 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 186 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072584","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A man buys 2 pencils for Rs. 5 and sells 5 pencils for Rs. 12. Find his gain or loss percent. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति 5 रुपये में 2 पेंसिल खरीदता है और 12 रुपये में 5 पेंसिल बेचता है। उसका लाभ या हानि प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4% gain","hi":"4% लाभ"},"2":{"en":"4% loss","hi":"4% हानि"},"3":{"en":"5% gain","hi":"5% लाभ"},"4":{"en":"5% loss","hi":"5% हानि"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"With 10 pencils, the cost price is 5 × Rs. 5 = Rs. 25, because 2 pencils cost Rs. 5<br>The selling price of 10 pencils is 2 × Rs. 12 = Rs. 24, because 5 pencils sell for Rs. 12<br>So there is a loss of 25 − 24 = Re. 1 on a cost of Rs. 25, which is 1 / 25 × 100 = 4%<br>Hence the loss percent is 4%<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4% loss.</b>","hi":"10 पेंसिलों पर लागत मूल्य 5 × 5 = 25 रुपये है, क्योंकि 2 पेंसिल 5 रुपये की हैं<br>10 पेंसिलों का विक्रय मूल्य 2 × 12 = 24 रुपये है, क्योंकि 5 पेंसिल 12 रुपये की बिकती हैं<br>अतः 25 रुपये की लागत पर 25 − 24 = 1 रुपये की हानि है, अर्थात् 1 / 25 × 100 = 4%<br>इसलिए हानि प्रतिशत 4% है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4% हानि है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072585","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Which of the following is/are identical to the address given:<br>Vill: Bhatgaon, PO: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494661<br>1. Vill: Bhatgaon, PO: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494661<br>2. Vill: Bhatgaon, Post: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494662<br>3. Vill: Bhatgaon, PO: Rajnandgaon, PS: Bilaspur, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494660<br>4. Village: Bhatgaon, PO: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494661 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा/से दिए गए पते के समान है/हैं:<br>Vill: Bhatgaon, PO: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494661<br>1. Vill: Bhatgaon, PO: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494661<br>2. Vill: Bhatgaon, Post: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494662<br>3. Vill: Bhatgaon, PO: Rajnandgaon, PS: Bilaspur, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494660<br>4. Village: Bhatgaon, PO: Ambikapur, PS: Rajnandgaon, Dist: Chhattisgarh &#8211; 494661 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 Only","hi":"केवल 2"},"2":{"en":"3 Only","hi":"केवल 3"},"3":{"en":"1 Only","hi":"केवल 1"},"4":{"en":"4 Only","hi":"केवल 4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The given address has PO Ambikapur, PS Rajnandgaon and the pin code 494661<br>Option 2 changes the pin code to 494662 and writes Post in place of PO, and option 3 changes the PO and the PS and the pin code to 494660<br>Option 4 writes Village in place of Vill but keeps every detail the same, and option 1 repeats the address word for word<br>Hence only option 1 is identical to the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1 Only.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में PO Ambikapur, PS Rajnandgaon तथा पिन कोड 494661 है<br>विकल्प 2 में पिन कोड 494662 है और PO के स्थान पर Post लिखा है, तथा विकल्प 3 में PO और PS बदले हुए हैं और पिन कोड 494660 है<br>विकल्प 4 में Vill के स्थान पर Village है परंतु शेष सभी विवरण वही हैं, और विकल्प 1 पते को शब्दशः दोहराता है<br>इसलिए केवल विकल्प 1 दिए गए पते के समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072586","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"<b>Statement:</b><br>All apples are fruits.<br>All fruits are healthy.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. All apples are healthy.<br>II. Some healthy things are fruits [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन:<br>सभी सेब फल हैं।<br>सभी फल स्वास्थ्यवर्धक हैं।<br>निष्कर्ष:<br>I. सभी सेब स्वास्थ्यवर्धक हैं।<br>II. कुछ स्वास्थ्यवर्धक चीज़ें फल हैं। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"All apples are fruits and all fruits are healthy, so every apple is healthy and conclusion I follows<br>All fruits are healthy means that fruits also lie inside the healthy group, so some healthy things are certainly fruits and conclusion II follows<br>Hence both conclusions I and II follow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Both I and II follow.</b>","hi":"सभी सेब फल हैं और सभी फल स्वास्थ्यवर्धक हैं, अतः प्रत्येक सेब स्वास्थ्यवर्धक है और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br>सभी फल स्वास्थ्यवर्धक हैं का अर्थ है कि फल स्वास्थ्यवर्धक समूह के भीतर भी हैं, अतः कुछ स्वास्थ्यवर्धक चीज़ें निश्चित रूप से फल हैं और निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>इसलिए निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): I और II दोनों निकलते हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072587","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code, \"HORSE\" is written as \"GNQRD\". How is PLANE written? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट में \"HORSE\" को \"GNQRD\" लिखा जाता है। PLANE कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"OKZMD"},"2":{"en":"OKZMF"},"3":{"en":"OKZND"},"4":{"en":"OKZNC"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In HORSE every letter moves one place back: H&#8594;G, O&#8594;N, R&#8594;Q, S&#8594;R and E&#8594;D, which gives GNQRD ✔<br>Applying the same step to PLANE: P&#8594;O, L&#8594;K, A&#8594;Z, N&#8594;M and E&#8594;D<br>Hence PLANE is written as OKZMD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): OKZMD.</b>","hi":"HORSE में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान पीछे जाता है: H&#8594;G, O&#8594;N, R&#8594;Q, S&#8594;R तथा E&#8594;D, जिससे GNQRD मिलता है ✔<br>PLANE पर वही चरण लगाने से P&#8594;O, L&#8594;K, A&#8594;Z, N&#8594;M तथा E&#8594;D<br>इसलिए PLANE को OKZMD लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): OKZMD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072588","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>128, 64, 32, ___ [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>128, 64, 32, ___ [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"18"},"4":{"en":"22"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Every term is half of the term before it: 128 ÷ 2 = 64 and 64 ÷ 2 = 32 ✔<br>So the next term is 32 ÷ 2 = 16<br>Hence the next number is 16<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पहले के पद का आधा है: 128 ÷ 2 = 64 तथा 64 ÷ 2 = 32 ✔<br>अतः अगला पद 32 ÷ 2 = 16 है<br>इसलिए अगली संख्या 16 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072589","section":"REASONING","topic":"Inequality","question":{"en":"In the question, assuming the given statements to be true, find which of the conclusion(s) among three conclusions is/are definitely true and then give your answer accordingly.<br><b>Statements:</b> R &gt; M &#8805; N = O &#8805; P; L &lt; S &lt; Q = K &#8804; P<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. M &gt; L<br>II. Q &#8804; M<br>III. S &lt; R [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"प्रश्न में दिए गए कथनों को सत्य मानते हुए ज्ञात कीजिए कि तीन निष्कर्षों में से कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष निश्चित रूप से सत्य है/हैं और तदनुसार उत्तर दीजिए।<br><b>कथन:</b> R &gt; M &#8805; N = O &#8805; P; L &lt; S &lt; Q = K &#8804; P<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. M &gt; L<br>II. Q &#8804; M<br>III. S &lt; R [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion II and III are true","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II और III सत्य हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion I is true","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I सत्य है"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I and II are true","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और II सत्य हैं"},"4":{"en":"All the conclusions I, II and III are true","hi":"निष्कर्ष I, II और III सभी सत्य हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The two statements together give L &lt; S &lt; Q = K &#8804; P &#8804; O = N &#8804; M &lt; R, so the full chain runs L &lt; S &lt; Q &#8804; M &lt; R<br>Since Q &#8804; M and M &lt; R, we get M &gt; L, so conclusion I is true ✔<br>Q &#8804; M comes straight from the chain, so conclusion II is true ✔<br>R is greater than M, and M is at least Q, which is greater than S, so S &lt; R and conclusion III is true ✔<br>Hence all the conclusions I, II and III are true<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): All the conclusions I, II and III are true.</b>","hi":"दोनों कथन मिलकर L &lt; S &lt; Q = K &#8804; P &#8804; O = N &#8804; M &lt; R देते हैं, अतः पूरी शृंखला L &lt; S &lt; Q &#8804; M &lt; R है<br>Q &#8804; M तथा M &lt; R से M &gt; L मिलता है, अतः निष्कर्ष I सत्य है ✔<br>Q &#8804; M शृंखला से सीधे मिलता है, अतः निष्कर्ष II सत्य है ✔<br>R, M से बड़ा है और M, Q से कम नहीं है, जो S से बड़ा है, अतः S &lt; R और निष्कर्ष III सत्य है ✔<br>इसलिए निष्कर्ष I, II और III सभी सत्य हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): निष्कर्ष I, II और III सभी सत्य हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072590","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If PLANTS is coded as QMBOUT, how is QMBOUT coded? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि PLANTS का कूट QMBOUT है, तो QMBOUT का कूट क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RNCPVU"},"2":{"en":"RNCPST"},"3":{"en":"RNDPVU"},"4":{"en":"RNCPUV"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In PLANTS every letter moves one place ahead: P&#8594;Q, L&#8594;M, A&#8594;B, N&#8594;O, T&#8594;U and S&#8594;T, which gives QMBOUT ✔<br>Applying the same step to QMBOUT: Q&#8594;R, M&#8594;N, B&#8594;C, O&#8594;P, U&#8594;V and T&#8594;U<br>Hence QMBOUT is coded as RNCPVU<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): RNCPVU.</b>","hi":"PLANTS में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे जाता है: P&#8594;Q, L&#8594;M, A&#8594;B, N&#8594;O, T&#8594;U तथा S&#8594;T, जिससे QMBOUT मिलता है ✔<br>QMBOUT पर वही चरण लगाने से Q&#8594;R, M&#8594;N, B&#8594;C, O&#8594;P, U&#8594;V तथा T&#8594;U<br>इसलिए QMBOUT का कूट RNCPVU है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): RNCPVU है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072591","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"UNDERSTAND\" is written as \"ENATSREDNV\". How will \"CONNECTION\" be written? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"UNDERSTAND\" को \"ENATSREDNV\" लिखा जाता है। \"CONNECTION\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"OOITCENNOD"},"2":{"en":"NOITCENNOC"},"3":{"en":"OIOTCENOND"},"4":{"en":"NOCITENONC"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"UNDERSTAND has 10 letters and its code ENATSREDNV is the word written backwards with its first and last letters moved one place ahead: the word backwards reads D N A T S R E D N U, and D becomes E while U becomes V, which gives E N A T S R E D N V ✔<br>Applying the same step to CONNECTION: the word backwards reads N O I T C E N N O C, and N becomes O while C becomes D, which gives O O I T C E N N O D<br>Hence CONNECTION is written as OOITCENNOD<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): OOITCENNOD.</b>","hi":"UNDERSTAND में 10 अक्षर हैं और उसका कूट ENATSREDNV शब्द को उल्टा लिखकर पहले तथा अंतिम अक्षर को एक स्थान आगे बढ़ाकर बनता है: शब्द उल्टा D N A T S R E D N U पढ़ा जाता है, D से E और U से V बनता है, जिससे E N A T S R E D N V मिलता है ✔<br>CONNECTION पर वही चरण लगाने से शब्द उल्टा N O I T C E N N O C पढ़ा जाता है, N से O और C से D बनता है, जिससे O O I T C E N N O D मिलता है<br>इसलिए CONNECTION को OOITCENNOD लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): OOITCENNOD है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072592","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 21Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America"},"2":{"en":"Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulvard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America"},"3":{"en":"Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60111United States of America"},"4":{"en":"Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The original address has Phase 12, Lincoln Boulevard and the zip code 60611<br>The first option changes the phase to 21, the second writes Boulvard and the third changes the zip code to 60111<br>Only the fourth option repeats the original address exactly<br>Hence the fourth option perfectly matches the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America.</b>","hi":"मूल पते में Phase 12, Lincoln Boulevard तथा ज़िप कोड 60611 है<br>पहले विकल्प में फेज़ 21 है, दूसरे में Boulvard लिखा है तथा तीसरे में ज़िप कोड 60111 है<br>केवल चौथा विकल्प मूल पते को ठीक वैसा ही दोहराता है<br>अतः चौथा विकल्प दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Flat No 27CImperial Heights Residency Phase 12Lincoln Boulevard Central AreaChicago Illinois 60611United States of America है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072593","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">1</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">4</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">2</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The third column of the matrix reads 1, 4 and 9, which are the squares of 1, 2 and 3, so the entries of the third column are consecutive perfect squares<br>The first two columns supply the base numbers: 3 + 6 = 9 = 3², 3 + 2 = 5 and 2 + 8 = 10, so no single arithmetic operation on the first two entries of a row reproduces the third entry of every row<br>Following the square pattern of the third column, the missing entry is 3² = 9<br>Hence the missing number is 9<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 9.</b>","hi":"आव्यूह का तीसरा स्तंभ 1, 4 तथा 9 पढ़ता है, जो 1, 2 तथा 3 के वर्ग हैं, अतः तीसरे स्तंभ के पद क्रमागत पूर्ण वर्ग हैं<br>पहले दो स्तंभ आधार संख्याएँ देते हैं: 3 + 6 = 9 = 3², 3 + 2 = 5 तथा 2 + 8 = 10, अतः पंक्ति के पहले दो पदों पर कोई एक गणितीय संक्रिया तीसरा पद नहीं देती<br>तीसरे स्तंभ के वर्ग पैटर्न के अनुसार लुप्त पद 3² = 9 है<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 9 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072594","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"A, B, C, D, E, and F constitute a family of six individuals. A shares a marital relationship with B, and A is the father of C. C is the son of B, whereas F is the daughter of C. E is the brother of C, and D is the sister of A. Using the given information, determine how many members of the family are female. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"A, B, C, D, E तथा F छह व्यक्तियों का एक परिवार हैं। A का B के साथ वैवाहिक संबंध है और A, C का पिता है। C, B का पुत्र है, जबकि F, C की पुत्री है। E, C का भाई है और D, A की बहन है। दी गई जानकारी के आधार पर निर्धारित कीजिए कि परिवार में कितने सदस्य महिला हैं। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A is the father of C and B is the mother of C, so A is male and B is female<br>C is male, E is his brother and is male, and F is the daughter of C and is female<br>D is the sister of A and is female<br>So the female members are B, F and D, that is three<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 19H118M34 25H118\"/><path d=\"M34 85H118M34 91H118\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H220V78\"/><path d=\"M76 94V121H28V144\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">F−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">F−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">E+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">E+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"A, C का पिता है तथा B, C की माता है, अतः A पुरुष और B महिला है<br>C पुरुष है, E उसका भाई है और पुरुष है, तथा F, C की पुत्री है और महिला है<br>D, A की बहन है और महिला है<br>अतः महिला सदस्य B, F तथा D अर्थात् तीन हैं<br><svg width=\"280\" height=\"196\" viewBox=\"0 0 280 196\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\" font-family=\"Georgia, serif\"><g stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M<path d=\"M34 19H118M34 25H118\"/><path d=\"M34 85H118M34 91H118\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H28V78\"/><path d=\"M76 28V55H220V78\"/><path d=\"M76 94V121H28V144\"/><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">A+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">A+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">B−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"26\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">B−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">C+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">C+</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">F−</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">F−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">D−</text><text x=\"220\" y=\"92\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">D−</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">E+</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"158\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"12\" fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\">E+</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3.2\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text><text x=\"6\" y=\"182\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"10\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></g></svg><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072595","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The roll number format is [Digit A]-[Digit B]-[Digit C] where C = (A+B) &#215; 2. Identify the inconsistent roll number. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रोल नंबर का प्रारूप [अंक A]-[अंक B]-[अंक C] है, जहाँ C = (A+B) &#215; 2 है। असंगत रोल नंबर पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-3-10"},"2":{"en":"4-1-10"},"3":{"en":"5-2-14"},"4":{"en":"6-2-18"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For 2-3-10, (2 + 3) × 2 = 10 ✔; for 4-1-10, (4 + 1) × 2 = 10 ✔ and for 5-2-14, (5 + 2) × 2 = 14 ✔<br>For 6-2-18, (6 + 2) × 2 = 16, but the code shows 18 ✘<br>Hence 6-2-18 is the inconsistent roll number<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 6-2-18.</b>","hi":"2-3-10 के लिए (2 + 3) × 2 = 10 ✔; 4-1-10 के लिए (4 + 1) × 2 = 10 ✔ तथा 5-2-14 के लिए (5 + 2) × 2 = 14 ✔<br>6-2-18 के लिए (6 + 2) × 2 = 16 है, परंतु कूट में 18 है ✘<br>इसलिए 6-2-18 असंगत रोल नंबर है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 6-2-18 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072596","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001 [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lt. Col. V.K Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001"},"2":{"en":"Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248002"},"3":{"en":"Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001"},"4":{"en":"Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt. Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The given entry has VK Singh without a full stop after V, the date 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area and the pin code 248001<br>The first option writes V.K Singh, the second changes the pin code to 248002 and the fourth writes Cantt. Area<br>Only the third option keeps every part exactly as it is printed<br>Hence the third option is exactly similar<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001.</b>","hi":"दी गई प्रविष्टि में V के बाद बिंदु के बिना VK Singh, तिथि 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area तथा पिन कोड 248001 है<br>पहले विकल्प में V.K Singh है, दूसरे में पिन कोड 248002 है तथा चौथे में Cantt. Area है<br>केवल तीसरा विकल्प प्रत्येक भाग को ठीक वैसा ही रखता है<br>अतः तीसरा विकल्प ठीक इसके समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): Lt. Col. VK Singh, 09 Jan 2011, Cantt Area, Dehradun (UK)-248001 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072597","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"A dedicated employee who recently went through a difficult personal divorce has shown a noticeable dip in accuracy over the last three weeks, missing two critical reporting deadlines. How should you address this situation to balance organisational accountability with emotional intelligence? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक समर्पित कर्मचारी, जो हाल ही में कठिन व्यक्तिगत तलाक से गुजरा है, पिछले तीन सप्ताह में शुद्धता में स्पष्ट गिरावट दिखा रहा है और दो महत्वपूर्ण रिपोर्टिंग समय-सीमाएँ चूक गया है। संगठनात्मक जवाबदेही तथा भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता के संतुलन के लिए आपको इस स्थिति को कैसे संबोधित करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Send a formal, strictly objective email detailing the missed deadlines and attaching the company's standard performance improvement policy guidelines.","hi":"चूकी गई समय-सीमाओं का विवरण देते हुए और कंपनी की मानक प्रदर्शन सुधार नीति संलग्न करते हुए औपचारिक, पूर्णतः वस्तुनिष्ठ ईमेल भेजना।"},"2":{"en":"Arrange a private discussion to appreciate past contributions, address recent gaps, and explore workflow improvements to stabilize performance.","hi":"निजी चर्चा का आयोजन करना, पिछले योगदान की सराहना करना, हाल की कमियों पर बात करना और प्रदर्शन स्थिर करने के लिए कार्यप्रवाह में सुधार खोजना।"},"3":{"en":"Avoid mentioning the missed deadlines entirely out of sympathy, and quietly distribute their pending tasks among the rest of the team.","hi":"सहानुभूति में चूकी गई समय-सीमाओं का उल्लेख पूरी तरह टालना और उनके लंबित कार्य चुपचाप शेष टीम में बाँट देना।"},"4":{"en":"Invite them for a coffee and tell them an extensive personal story about how you successfully handled your own past personal crises to motivate them.","hi":"उन्हें कॉफ़ी पर बुलाकर अपने पिछले व्यक्तिगत संकटों को सफलतापूर्वक संभालने की लंबी व्यक्तिगत कहानी सुनाकर उन्हें प्रेरित करना।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The missed deadlines are a real accountability issue, and the employee's personal trouble is real too, so both must be handled together<br>A private talk that first recognises past contributions, then speaks clearly about the recent gaps and then looks for workflow fixes gives support while keeping the standard intact<br>A formal email alone ignores the human side, hiding the delay shifts the cost to the team, and telling one's own story does not fix the work<br>Hence a private discussion with appreciation, clarity about gaps and workflow improvement is the right balance<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Arrange a private discussion to appreciate past contributions, address recent gaps, and explore workflow improvements to stabilize performance..</b>","hi":"चूकी गई समय-सीमाएँ वास्तविक जवाबदेही का मामला हैं और कर्मचारी की व्यक्तिगत परेशानी भी वास्तविक है, अतः दोनों को साथ संभालना चाहिए<br>निजी बातचीत में पहले पिछले योगदान की सराहना, फिर हाल की कमियों पर स्पष्ट बात और फिर कार्यप्रवाह में सुधार खोजना — यह सहयोग भी देता है और मानक भी बनाए रखता है<br>केवल औपचारिक ईमेल मानवीय पक्ष को अनदेखा करता है, देरी छिपाने से भार टीम पर जाता है, और अपनी कहानी सुनाने से काम नहीं सुधरता<br>अतः सराहना, कमियों पर स्पष्टता तथा कार्यप्रवाह में सुधार वाली निजी चर्चा सही संतुलन है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): निजी चर्चा का आयोजन करना, पिछले योगदान की सराहना करना, हाल की कमियों पर बात करना और प्रदर्शन स्थिर करने के लिए कार्यप्रवाह में सुधार खोजना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072598","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a high-stakes strategy meeting, your department head proposes a plan you know is doomed to fail because it ignores ground-level data you recently processed. The room is silent; everyone is nodding along because they are afraid to challenge the boss. Your boss looks at you and asks: \"You have been quiet, do you agree that this is the best path forward?\" What is the most emotionally intelligent way to deliver a counterview without becoming a \"troublemaker\"? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अत्यंत महत्वपूर्ण रणनीति बैठक में आपका विभागाध्यक्ष एक ऐसी योजना प्रस्तावित करता है जिसके विफल होने का आपको पता है, क्योंकि यह उस ज़मीनी आँकड़ों को अनदेखा करती है जिन्हें आपने हाल ही में संसाधित किया है। कक्ष में सन्नाटा है; सभी बॉस को चुनौती देने के डर से सहमति में सिर हिला रहे हैं। आपका बॉस आपकी ओर देखकर पूछता है: \"आप चुप रहे, क्या आप सहमत हैं कि यह सर्वोत्तम मार्ग है?\" \"मुसीबत पैदा करने वाला\" बने बिना तर्क प्रस्तुत करने का सर्वाधिक भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता वाला तरीका क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\"I agree the plan is excellent, but I think we should wait for more data before starting. (A white lie to protect the peace).\"","hi":"\"मैं मानता हूँ कि योजना उत्कृष्ट है, परंतु मुझे लगता है कि शुरू करने से पहले अधिक आँकड़ों की प्रतीक्षा करनी चाहिए। (शांति बनाए रखने के लिए एक छोटा झूठ)।\""},"2":{"en":"\"The data suggests this plan may not work as expected; we might need to reconsider.\"","hi":"\"आँकड़े बताते हैं कि यह योजना अपेक्षा के अनुसार काम नहीं कर सकती; हमें पुनर्विचार करना पड़ सकता है।\""},"3":{"en":"\"I see the logic in this goal, but recent data suggests a week-four bottleneck. Can we add a quick risk-mitigation step in phase one?\"","hi":"\"मुझे इस लक्ष्य का तर्क समझ आता है, परंतु हाल के आँकड़े चौथे सप्ताह में अवरोध दर्शाते हैं। क्या हम पहले चरण में एक त्वरित जोखिम-निवारण कदम जोड़ सकते हैं?\""},"4":{"en":"Stay silent and nod, as it is not your place to speak against the department head.","hi":"चुप रहकर सिर हिलाना, क्योंकि विभागाध्यक्ष के विरुद्ध बोलना आपका स्थान नहीं है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A counterview works best when it respects the superior's goal and adds a fact instead of rejecting the plan<br>The third response accepts the logic of the goal, brings in the recent data as a specific bottleneck and offers a small addition to the plan, so the boss can change course without losing face<br>Agreeing falsely, making a vague objection or staying silent all fail either the truth or the relationship<br>Hence the third response is the most emotionally intelligent way<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \"I see the logic in this goal, but recent data suggests a week-four bottleneck. Can we add a quick risk-mitigation step in phase one?\".</b>","hi":"तर्क तभी कारगर होता है जब वह वरिष्ठ के लक्ष्य का सम्मान करे और योजना को अस्वीकार करने के बजाय एक तथ्य जोड़े<br>तीसरा उत्तर लक्ष्य के तर्क को स्वीकार करता है, हाल के आँकड़ों को विशिष्ट अवरोध के रूप में सामने रखता है और योजना में एक छोटा जोड़ सुझाता है, जिससे बॉस को प्रतिष्ठा खोए बिना मार्ग बदलने की सुविधा मिलती है<br>झूठी सहमति, अस्पष्ट आपत्ति या चुप्पी — ये सत्य या संबंध दोनों में से कुछ न कुछ गँवा देते हैं<br>अतः तीसरा उत्तर सर्वाधिक भावनात्मक बुद्धिमत्ता वाला तरीका है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \"मुझे इस लक्ष्य का तर्क समझ आता है, परंतु हाल के आँकड़े चौथे सप्ताह में अवरोध दर्शाते हैं। क्या हम पहले चरण में एक त्वरित जोखिम-निवारण कदम जोड़ सकते हैं?\" है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072599","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>MNO : PQR :: STU : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>MNO : PQR :: STU : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"WXY"},"2":{"en":"UVW"},"3":{"en":"XYZ"},"4":{"en":"VWX"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each letter of MNO moves three places ahead to give PQR, and the same relation holds for the whole group<br>So STU moves three places ahead letter by letter: S&#8594;V, T&#8594;W and U&#8594;X<br>Hence the answer is VWX<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): VWX.</b>","hi":"MNO का प्रत्येक अक्षर तीन स्थान आगे जाकर PQR देता है, और यही संबंध पूरे समूह पर लागू होता है<br>अतः STU के प्रत्येक अक्षर को तीन स्थान आगे बढ़ाने पर S&#8594;V, T&#8594;W तथा U&#8594;X<br>इसलिए उत्तर VWX है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): VWX है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072600","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 8 &#9733; 4 # 5 = 10 and 18 &#9733; 3 # 2 = 12, then what will be the value of 32 &#9733; 4 # 6? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि 8 &#9733; 4 # 5 = 10 तथा 18 &#9733; 3 # 2 = 12 है, तो 32 &#9733; 4 # 6 का मान क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"48"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"52"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The pattern is (first &#247; second) + third × 1: 8 ÷ 4 + 5 = 2 + 5 = 7 ✘, so check the multiplication form: (first &#247; second) × third ÷ 1 gives 8 ÷ 4 × 5 = 10 ✔ and 18 ÷ 3 × 2 = 12 ✔<br>So the rule is first &#247; second × third<br>Applying it, 32 ÷ 4 × 6 = 8 × 6 = 48<br>Hence the value is 48<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 48.</b>","hi":"नियम है पहली संख्या ÷ दूसरी संख्या × तीसरी संख्या: 8 ÷ 4 × 5 = 10 ✔ तथा 18 ÷ 3 × 2 = 12 ✔<br>अतः 32 ÷ 4 × 6 = 8 × 6 = 48<br>इसलिए मान 48 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 48 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072601","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Sarah wants to open a high-end bakery in a bustling part of the city. She needs a location that gets heavy weekend pedestrian traffic and is near other lifestyle shops. Which of given options should she select? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सारा शहर के व्यस्त हिस्से में एक उच्च-स्तरीय बेकरी खोलना चाहती है। उसे ऐसा स्थान चाहिए जहाँ सप्ताहांत पर भारी पैदल आवागमन हो और जो अन्य जीवनशैली दुकानों के निकट हो। दिए गए विकल्पों में से उसे कौन-सा चुनना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A quiet corner shop in a suburban area that is rarely visited on the weekends.","hi":"उपनगरीय क्षेत्र में एक शांत कोने की दुकान, जहाँ सप्ताहांत पर शायद ही कोई आता है।"},"2":{"en":"A small booth situated in a busy food court inside a popular weekend mall.","hi":"एक लोकप्रिय सप्ताहांत मॉल के भीतर व्यस्त फ़ूड कोर्ट में स्थित एक छोटा बूथ।"},"3":{"en":"A store in a remote business park that is closed on all weekend afternoons.","hi":"एक दूरस्थ बिज़नेस पार्क में दुकान, जो सप्ताहांत की सभी दोपहरों में बंद रहता है।"},"4":{"en":"A basement unit in a large office building with no nearby retail presence.","hi":"एक बड़ी कार्यालय इमारत में बेसमेंट इकाई, जिसके आसपास कोई खुदरा उपस्थिति नहीं है।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A high-end bakery needs many weekend walk-in customers and nearby lifestyle shops that bring the same kind of buyers<br>A booth in a busy food court of a popular weekend mall sits exactly in that crowd and next to other shops ✔<br>The quiet suburban corner, the closed business park and the basement with no retail around all cut off the footfall Sarah needs<br>Hence the small booth in the busy food court of a popular weekend mall is the right choice<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A small booth situated in a busy food court inside a popular weekend mall..</b>","hi":"उच्च-स्तरीय बेकरी को सप्ताहांत पर अनेक पैदल ग्राहक तथा आस-पास ऐसी जीवनशैली दुकानें चाहिए जो वही खरीदार लाएँ<br>लोकप्रिय सप्ताहांत मॉल के व्यस्त फ़ूड कोर्ट में बूथ ठीक उसी भीड़ में और अन्य दुकानों के बगल में है ✔<br>शांत उपनगरीय कोना, बंद बिज़नेस पार्क तथा आसपास खुदरा के बिना बेसमेंट — ये सभी आवश्यक पैदल आवागमन काट देते हैं<br>अतः लोकप्रिय सप्ताहांत मॉल के व्यस्त फ़ूड कोर्ट में छोटा बूथ सही चुनाव है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): एक लोकप्रिय सप्ताहांत मॉल के भीतर व्यस्त फ़ूड कोर्ट में स्थित एक छोटा बूथ। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072602","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You notice that a coworker has been consistently arriving late and leaving early, and another colleague jokes that they should \"get caught\" by the boss. You're not in a supervisory role. What's the best response? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"आप देखते हैं कि एक सहकर्मी लगातार देर से आ रहा है और जल्दी चला जाता है, और दूसरा सहकर्मी मज़ाक में कहता है कि वह \"बॉस की नज़र में\" आ जाए। आप पर्यवेक्षक की भूमिका में नहीं हैं। सर्वोत्तम प्रतिक्रिया क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Join the joke, since it's harmless office banter.","hi":"मज़ाक में शामिल हो जाना, क्योंकि यह हानिरहित दफ़्तरी मज़ाक है।"},"2":{"en":"Mention it to the boss yourself so the issue gets addressed.","hi":"स्वयं बॉस को बता देना ताकि मामला सुलझ जाए।"},"3":{"en":"Avoid gossip and focus on your own responsibilities.","hi":"गपशप से बचना और अपनी ज़िम्मेदारियों पर ध्यान देना।"},"4":{"en":"Confront the coworker directly about their attendance.","hi":"सहकर्मी से सीधे उसकी उपस्थिति के बारे में बात करना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"It is not your role to monitor a colleague's timing, and joining the joke or carrying the matter to the boss damages trust without any real benefit<br>Talking to the coworker about their attendance or reporting them also crosses the line of your role<br>Staying away from gossip and doing your own work keeps the workplace healthy and is the right response<br>Hence avoiding gossip and focusing on your own responsibilities is the best response<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Avoid gossip and focus on your own responsibilities..</b>","hi":"सहकर्मी के समय की निगरानी आपकी भूमिका नहीं है, और मज़ाक में शामिल होना या बात बॉस तक पहुँचाना बिना लाभ के भरोसा तोड़ता है<br>सहकर्मी से उपस्थिति पर बात करना या उसकी शिकायत करना भी आपकी भूमिका की सीमा पार करना है<br>गपशप से दूर रहकर अपना काम करना कार्यस्थल को स्वस्थ रखता है और सही प्रतिक्रिया है<br>अतः गपशप से बचना और अपनी ज़िम्मेदारियों पर ध्यान देना सर्वोत्तम प्रतिक्रिया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): गपशप से बचना और अपनी ज़िम्मेदारियों पर ध्यान देना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072603","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>An IT organization has deployed advanced encryption protocols and intrusion detection systems to strengthen its cybersecurity framework.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Cyberattacks have been eliminated in all systems.<br>II. Encryption alone is sufficient to prevent all security breaches. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक आईटी संगठन ने अपने साइबर सुरक्षा ढाँचे को मजबूत करने के लिए उन्नत एन्क्रिप्शन प्रोटोकॉल तथा घुसपैठ पहचान प्रणालियाँ तैनात की हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. सभी प्रणालियों में साइबर हमले समाप्त हो गए हैं।<br>II. सभी सुरक्षा उल्लंघनों को रोकने के लिए एन्क्रिप्शन अकेला ही पर्याप्त है। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement says that the framework has been strengthened, not that every attack has stopped, so conclusion I goes far beyond the statement<br>The organisation has used both encryption and intrusion detection, which shows that encryption alone is not treated as enough, so conclusion II is also not supported<br>Hence neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन कहता है कि ढाँचा मजबूत किया गया है, यह नहीं कि हर हमला रुक गया, अतः निष्कर्ष I कथन से बहुत आगे बढ़ जाता है<br>संगठन ने एन्क्रिप्शन तथा घुसपैठ पहचान दोनों का प्रयोग किया है, जिससे दिखता है कि एन्क्रिप्शन अकेले को पर्याप्त नहीं माना गया, अतः निष्कर्ष II भी समर्थित नहीं है<br>इसलिए न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072604","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word.<br>Lion : Den :: Rabbit : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है।<br>Lion : Den :: Rabbit : ? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hole","hi":"बिल"},"2":{"en":"Burrow","hi":"खरगोशदर"},"3":{"en":"Stable","hi":"अस्तबल"},"4":{"en":"Kennel","hi":"कुत्ताघर"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A den is the place where a lion lives<br>In the same way the place where a rabbit lives is a burrow ✔<br>A hole is a general word, a stable is for horses and a kennel is for dogs<br>Hence the answer is Burrow<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Burrow.</b>","hi":"Den वह स्थान है जहाँ शेर रहता है<br>उसी प्रकार खरगोश जहाँ रहता है वह स्थान burrow है ✔<br>Hole एक सामान्य शब्द है, stable घोड़ों के लिए और kennel कुत्तों के लिए होता है<br>इसलिए उत्तर Burrow है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): खरगोशदर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072605","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A leading nutrition brand has claimed that its new plant-based protein shake is the most effective supplement for muscle recovery.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. All other protein supplements currently on the market are ineffective for muscle recovery.<br>II. Consumers will believe the company's claim without checking independent scientific studies. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक प्रमुख पोषण ब्रांड ने दावा किया है कि उसका नया प्लांट-आधारित प्रोटीन शेक मांसपेशियों की रिकवरी के लिए सबसे प्रभावी सप्लीमेंट है।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. बाज़ार में उपलब्ध अन्य सभी प्रोटीन सप्लीमेंट मांसपेशियों की रिकवरी के लिए अप्रभावी हैं।<br>II. उपभोक्ता स्वतंत्र वैज्ञानिक अध्ययन जाँचे बिना कंपनी के दावे पर विश्वास कर लेंगे। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The claim says that the shake is the most effective, which only means it is better than the others, not that all the others are ineffective, so assumption I is too strong<br>A company advertises a claim like this whether or not buyers check the studies, so the statement does not depend on assumption II either<br>Hence neither assumption I nor II is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit.</b>","hi":"दावा कहता है कि शेक सबसे प्रभावी है, जिसका अर्थ केवल यह है कि वह अन्य से बेहतर है, यह नहीं कि अन्य सभी अप्रभावी हैं, अतः अवधारणा I अत्यधिक है<br>कंपनी ऐसा दावा इस बात पर निर्भर नहीं करती कि खरीदार अध्ययन जाँचते हैं या नहीं, अतः कथन अवधारणा II पर भी निर्भर नहीं है<br>इसलिए न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072606","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"Aurangzeb issued the Fatawa-i-Alamgiri in which year? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"औरंगज़ेब ने फ़तवा-ए-आलमगीरी किस वर्ष जारी किया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1675 CE","hi":"1675 ई."},"2":{"en":"1667 CE","hi":"1667 ई."},"3":{"en":"1680 CE","hi":"1680 ई."},"4":{"en":"1670 CE","hi":"1670 ई."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1675 CE</b><br>The <b>Fatawa-i-Alamgiri</b>, a compilation of <b>Hanafi Islamic law</b> prepared by a board of jurists under Aurangzeb's patronage, is dated to <b><u>1675 CE</u></b> in standard exam references.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The compilation was headed by <b>Shaikh Nizam Burhanpuri</b>.<br>• Aurangzeb re-imposed <b>jizya in 1679</b> and banned music at the court.<br>• Aurangzeb was called <b>\"Zinda Pir\"</b>; his tomb is at <b>Khuldabad</b> (Maharashtra).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 1675 ई.</b><br><b>फ़तवा-ए-आलमगीरी</b>, औरंगज़ेब के संरक्षण में विधिवेत्ताओं के एक मंडल द्वारा तैयार <b>हनफ़ी इस्लामी कानून</b> का संकलन, मानक परीक्षा संदर्भों में <b><u>1675 ई.</u></b> का माना जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस संकलन का नेतृत्व <b>शेख निज़ाम बुरहानपुरी</b> ने किया।<br>• औरंगज़ेब ने <b>1679 में जज़िया</b> पुनः लगाया और दरबार में संगीत पर रोक लगाई।<br>• औरंगज़ेब को <b>\"ज़िंदा पीर\"</b> कहा जाता था; उसका मकबरा <b>खुल्दाबाद</b> (महाराष्ट्र) में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072607","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"What does IMEC stand for? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"IMEC का पूर्ण रूप क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Indian Maritime Economic Council","hi":"भारतीय समुद्री आर्थिक परिषद"},"2":{"en":"India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor","hi":"भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा"},"3":{"en":"International Monetary Economic Committee","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय मौद्रिक आर्थिक समिति"},"4":{"en":"Indo-Mediterranean Export Corporation","hi":"भारत-भूमध्यसागरीय निर्यात निगम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor</b><br><b>IMEC</b> stands for <b><u>India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor</u></b>, announced on the sidelines of the <b>G20 New Delhi Summit (September 2023)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• MoU signatories: <b>India, USA, Saudi Arabia, UAE, EU, France, Germany and Italy</b>.<br>• It has an <b>Eastern Corridor</b> (India–Gulf) and a <b>Northern Corridor</b> (Gulf–Europe).<br>• Seen as an alternative to China's <b>Belt and Road Initiative (BRI)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा</b><br><b>IMEC</b> का पूर्ण रूप <b><u>भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा</u></b> है, जिसकी घोषणा <b>G20 नई दिल्ली शिखर सम्मेलन (सितंबर 2023)</b> के दौरान की गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• MoU हस्ताक्षरकर्ता: <b>भारत, अमेरिका, सऊदी अरब, UAE, यूरोपीय संघ, फ्रांस, जर्मनी और इटली</b>।<br>• इसमें <b>पूर्वी गलियारा</b> (भारत–खाड़ी) और <b>उत्तरी गलियारा</b> (खाड़ी–यूरोप) है।<br>• इसे चीन की <b>बेल्ट एंड रोड पहल (BRI)</b> का विकल्प माना जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072608","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"What is the main form of transportation that will be used within the IMEC (India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor) corridor? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"IMEC (भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा) गलियारे में मुख्य रूप से परिवहन के किस साधन का उपयोग किया जाएगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Air travel","hi":"हवाई यात्रा"},"2":{"en":"Maritime and Rail","hi":"समुद्री और रेल"},"3":{"en":"Solely road transport","hi":"केवल सड़क परिवहन"},"4":{"en":"Solely space travel","hi":"केवल अंतरिक्ष यात्रा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Maritime and Rail</b><br>IMEC is a <b><u>multimodal ship-to-rail network</u></b>: goods go by sea from India to the UAE, by rail across Saudi Arabia and Jordan to Israel, and again by sea to Europe.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Key ports: <b>Mundra, Kandla, JNPT</b> (India), <b>Haifa</b> (Israel), <b>Piraeus</b> (Greece).<br>• The corridor will also carry <b>electricity cables, hydrogen pipelines and digital cables</b>.<br>• It is expected to cut transit time to Europe by about <b>40%</b> compared to the Suez route.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – समुद्री और रेल</b><br>IMEC एक <b><u>बहु-मॉडल जहाज़-से-रेल नेटवर्क</u></b> है: माल भारत से UAE तक समुद्र से, सऊदी अरब और जॉर्डन होते हुए इज़राइल तक रेल से, और फिर समुद्र से यूरोप पहुँचेगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• प्रमुख बंदरगाह: <b>मुंद्रा, कांडला, JNPT</b> (भारत), <b>हाइफ़ा</b> (इज़राइल), <b>पीरियस</b> (ग्रीस)।<br>• गलियारे में <b>बिजली केबल, हाइड्रोजन पाइपलाइन और डिजिटल केबल</b> भी होंगे।<br>• स्वेज़ मार्ग की तुलना में यूरोप तक पारगमन समय लगभग <b>40%</b> कम होने की उम्मीद है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072609","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian sport involves riding a horse and attempting to spear a small target? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस भारतीय खेल में घुड़सवारी करते हुए एक छोटे लक्ष्य को भाले से भेदने का प्रयास किया जाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Polo","hi":"पोलो"},"2":{"en":"Tent Pegging","hi":"टेंट पेगिंग"},"3":{"en":"Jousting","hi":"जूस्टिंग"},"4":{"en":"Rodeo","hi":"रोडियो"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Tent Pegging</b><br>In <b><u>Tent Pegging</u></b>, a rider at full gallop uses a <b>lance or sword</b> to pierce and carry away a small ground target (peg).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Tent pegging is a cavalry sport, popular in the <b>Indian Army</b> (61<sup>st</sup> Cavalry).<br>• <b>Polo</b> originated in <b>Manipur</b> (Sagol Kangjei); Imphal's polo ground is among the oldest.<br>• <b>Jousting</b> is a medieval European sport; <b>Rodeo</b> is associated with the USA.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – टेंट पेगिंग</b><br><b><u>टेंट पेगिंग</u></b> में घुड़सवार तेज़ दौड़ते घोड़े पर <b>भाले या तलवार</b> से ज़मीन पर रखे छोटे लक्ष्य (खूँटी) को भेदकर उठा ले जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टेंट पेगिंग घुड़सवार सेना का खेल है, जो <b>भारतीय सेना</b> (61वीं कैवेलरी) में लोकप्रिय है।<br>• <b>पोलो</b> की उत्पत्ति <b>मणिपुर</b> (सगोल कंगजेई) में हुई।<br>• <b>जूस्टिंग</b> मध्यकालीन यूरोपीय खेल है; <b>रोडियो</b> अमेरिका से जुड़ा है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072610","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Who among the following received the DSC Prize for South Asian Literature in 2016 for Sleeping on Jupiter? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किसे 2016 में 'स्लीपिंग ऑन जुपिटर' के लिए दक्षिण एशियाई साहित्य का DSC पुरस्कार मिला? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Anuradha Roy","hi":"अनुराधा रॉय"},"2":{"en":"Arundhati Roy","hi":"अरुंधति रॉय"},"3":{"en":"Perumal Murugan","hi":"पेरुमल मुरुगन"},"4":{"en":"Jhumpa Lahiri","hi":"झुम्पा लाहिड़ी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Anuradha Roy</b><br><b><u>Anuradha Roy</u></b> won the <b>DSC Prize for South Asian Literature 2016</b> for her novel <b>Sleeping on Jupiter</b>, which was also longlisted for the Man Booker Prize 2015.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• DSC Prize was instituted in <b>2010</b>; first winner was <b>H.M. Naqvi</b> (Home Boy).<br>• <b>Arundhati Roy</b> – Booker Prize 1997 for <b>The God of Small Things</b>.<br>• <b>Jhumpa Lahiri</b> – Pulitzer Prize 2000 for <b>Interpreter of Maladies</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – अनुराधा रॉय</b><br><b><u>अनुराधा रॉय</u></b> को उनके उपन्यास <b>स्लीपिंग ऑन जुपिटर (Sleeping on Jupiter)</b> के लिए <b>2016 का DSC दक्षिण एशियाई साहित्य पुरस्कार</b> मिला; यह 2015 के मैन बुकर पुरस्कार की लंबी सूची में भी था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• DSC पुरस्कार <b>2010</b> में शुरू हुआ; पहले विजेता <b>एच.एम. नक़वी</b> (होम बॉय) थे।<br>• <b>अरुंधति रॉय</b> – <b>द गॉड ऑफ स्मॉल थिंग्स</b> के लिए 1997 का बुकर पुरस्कार।<br>• <b>झुम्पा लाहिड़ी</b> – <b>इंटरप्रेटर ऑफ मैलडीज़</b> के लिए 2000 का पुलित्ज़र पुरस्कार।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072611","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: National Organisations","question":{"en":"Which of the following commissions was set up in the year 1957 to foster the development of nuclear energy in India? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में परमाणु ऊर्जा के विकास को बढ़ावा देने के लिए वर्ष 1957 में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा आयोग स्थापित किया गया था? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Central Electricity Authority","hi":"केंद्रीय विद्युत प्राधिकरण"},"2":{"en":"Atomic Energy Commission","hi":"परमाणु ऊर्जा आयोग"},"3":{"en":"Finance Commission","hi":"वित्त आयोग"},"4":{"en":"Scientific Advisory Committee","hi":"वैज्ञानिक सलाहकार समिति"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Atomic Energy Commission</b><br>The <b><u>Atomic Energy Commission</u></b> is the apex body that frames policy for the development of <b>nuclear energy</b> in India; it was set up under <b>Dr. Homi J. Bhabha</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The AEC was first set up in <b>August 1948</b> and reconstituted under the <b>Department of Atomic Energy</b> in <b>1958</b>.<br>• The <b>Atomic Energy Establishment, Trombay</b> was set up in <b>1957</b>; renamed <b>BARC</b> in 1967.<br>• India's first nuclear reactor <b>Apsara</b> became critical in <b>1956</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – परमाणु ऊर्जा आयोग</b><br><b><u>परमाणु ऊर्जा आयोग (Atomic Energy Commission)</u></b> भारत में <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा</b> के विकास की नीति बनाने वाला शीर्ष निकाय है; इसकी स्थापना <b>डॉ. होमी जे. भाभा</b> के नेतृत्व में हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• AEC पहली बार <b>अगस्त 1948</b> में बना और <b>1958</b> में <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा विभाग</b> के अधीन पुनर्गठित हुआ।<br>• <b>परमाणु ऊर्जा प्रतिष्ठान, ट्रॉम्बे</b> <b>1957</b> में स्थापित हुआ; 1967 में इसका नाम <b>BARC</b> रखा गया।<br>• भारत का पहला परमाणु रिएक्टर <b>अप्सरा</b> <b>1956</b> में क्रांतिक हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072612","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which Irish author won the Booker Prize in 2005 for “The Sea”? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किस आयरिश लेखक ने 2005 में “द सी” के लिए बुकर पुरस्कार जीता? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Roddy Doyle","hi":"रॉडी डॉयल"},"2":{"en":"John Banville","hi":"जॉन बैनविल"},"3":{"en":"Colm Toibin","hi":"कॉल्म टॉयबिन"},"4":{"en":"Sebastian Barry","hi":"सेबेस्टियन बैरी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – John Banville</b><br>Irish novelist <b><u>John Banville</u></b> won the <b>Man Booker Prize 2005</b> for <b>The Sea</b>, a novel about a widower revisiting a seaside village of his childhood.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Roddy Doyle</b> won the Booker in <b>1993</b> for <b>Paddy Clarke Ha Ha Ha</b>.<br>• Booker Prize was first awarded in <b>1969</b>; the <b>International Booker</b> is for translated fiction.<br>• Indian winners: <b>Arundhati Roy (1997), Kiran Desai (2006), Aravind Adiga (2008)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – जॉन बैनविल</b><br>आयरिश उपन्यासकार <b><u>जॉन बैनविल</u></b> ने <b>द सी (The Sea)</b> के लिए <b>2005 का मैन बुकर पुरस्कार</b> जीता; यह अपने बचपन के समुद्र तटीय गाँव लौटे एक विधुर की कहानी है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>रॉडी डॉयल</b> ने <b>1993</b> में <b>पैडी क्लार्क हा हा हा</b> के लिए बुकर जीता।<br>• बुकर पुरस्कार पहली बार <b>1969</b> में दिया गया; <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बुकर</b> अनूदित कथा-साहित्य के लिए है।<br>• भारतीय विजेता: <b>अरुंधति रॉय (1997), किरण देसाई (2006), अरविंद अडिगा (2008)</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072613","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In which year was Kho-Kho included in the South Asian Games? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"खो-खो को दक्षिण एशियाई खेलों में किस वर्ष शामिल किया गया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2014"},"2":{"en":"2016"},"3":{"en":"2019"},"4":{"en":"2022"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 2016</b><br>Kho-Kho was included for the first time in the <b>12<sup>th</sup> South Asian Games</b> held at <b>Guwahati and Shillong</b> in <b><u>2016</u></b>, and India won gold in both men's and women's events.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The first <b>Kho-Kho World Cup</b> was held in <b>New Delhi in January 2025</b>; India won both men's and women's titles.<br>• Kho-Kho is played with <b>12 players</b> per side, of whom <b>9</b> take the field.<br>• Governing body in India: <b>Kho-Kho Federation of India</b> (1955).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 2016</b><br>खो-खो को <b>2016</b> में <b>गुवाहाटी और शिलांग</b> में आयोजित <b>12वें दक्षिण एशियाई खेलों</b> में शामिल किया गया, जहाँ भारत ने पुरुष और महिला दोनों वर्गों में स्वर्ण जीता: <b><u>2016</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पहला <b>खो-खो विश्व कप</b> <b>जनवरी 2025 में नई दिल्ली</b> में हुआ; भारत ने पुरुष और महिला दोनों खिताब जीते।<br>• खो-खो में प्रत्येक टीम में <b>12 खिलाड़ी</b> होते हैं, जिनमें से <b>9</b> मैदान में उतरते हैं।<br>• भारत में शासी निकाय: <b>खो-खो फेडरेशन ऑफ इंडिया</b> (1955)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072614","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The primary aim of the \"Land Revenue Policy\" introduced by the British in India was to: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अंग्रेज़ों द्वारा भारत में लागू \"भू-राजस्व नीति\" का प्राथमिक उद्देश्य था: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Promote the welfare and prosperity of Indian farmers.","hi":"भारतीय किसानों के कल्याण और समृद्धि को बढ़ावा देना।"},"2":{"en":"Establish a fair and equitable system of land ownership.","hi":"भूमि स्वामित्व की निष्पक्ष और न्यायसंगत व्यवस्था स्थापित करना।"},"3":{"en":"Maximize the revenue collected from land for the British government.","hi":"ब्रिटिश सरकार के लिए भूमि से अधिकतम राजस्व एकत्र करना।"},"4":{"en":"Encourage the cultivation of food crops to ensure food security.","hi":"खाद्य सुरक्षा के लिए खाद्य फसलों की खेती को प्रोत्साहित करना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Maximize the revenue collected from land for the British government.</b><br>British land revenue systems were designed to <b><u>maximise and secure the revenue from land</u></b> for the Company, which led to high assessments, peasant indebtedness and frequent famines.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>Permanent Settlement</b> (1793)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Lord Cornwallis – Bengal, Bihar, Odisha</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>Ryotwari</b> (1820)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Thomas Munro – Madras, Bombay</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>Mahalwari</b> (1822)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Holt Mackenzie – NW Provinces, Punjab</td></tr></table><br>• Under the Permanent Settlement, <b>zamindars</b> were made owners of land.<br>• Under Ryotwari, revenue was fixed directly with the <b>ryot (cultivator)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ब्रिटिश सरकार के लिए भूमि से अधिकतम राजस्व एकत्र करना।</b><br>ब्रिटिश भू-राजस्व व्यवस्थाएँ कंपनी के लिए <b><u>भूमि से अधिकतम और सुनिश्चित राजस्व</u></b> प्राप्त करने हेतु बनाई गई थीं, जिससे भारी लगान, किसानों की ऋणग्रस्तता और बार-बार अकाल पड़े।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br><table><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>स्थायी बंदोबस्त</b> (1793)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">लॉर्ड कॉर्नवालिस – बंगाल, बिहार, ओडिशा</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>रैयतवाड़ी</b> (1820)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">थॉमस मुनरो – मद्रास, बंबई</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\"><b>महालवाड़ी</b> (1822)</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">होल्ट मैकेंज़ी – उत्तर-पश्चिमी प्रांत, पंजाब</td></tr></table><br>• स्थायी बंदोबस्त में <b>ज़मींदारों</b> को भूमि का स्वामी बनाया गया।<br>• रैयतवाड़ी में राजस्व सीधे <b>रैयत (किसान)</b> से तय होता था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072615","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"What of the following is a major reform in the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita regarding FIRs (First Information Reports)? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"FIR (प्रथम सूचना रिपोर्ट) के संबंध में भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा प्रमुख सुधार है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"FIRs can no longer be filed","hi":"FIR अब दर्ज नहीं की जा सकती"},"2":{"en":"FIRs will now require court approval first","hi":"FIR के लिए अब पहले न्यायालय की स्वीकृति आवश्यक होगी"},"3":{"en":"FIRs can be filed online and via electronic communication","hi":"FIR ऑनलाइन और इलेक्ट्रॉनिक संचार के माध्यम से दर्ज की जा सकती है"},"4":{"en":"FIRs must be handwritten only","hi":"FIR केवल हस्तलिखित होनी चाहिए"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – FIRs can be filed online and via electronic communication</b><br><b>Section 173 of BNSS, 2023</b> allows information about a cognizable offence to be given by <b><u>electronic communication</u></b> (e-FIR); it must be signed by the informant within <b>3 days</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BNSS also provides for <b>Zero FIR</b> – an FIR can be lodged at any police station irrespective of jurisdiction.<br>• BNSS replaced the <b>CrPC, 1973</b> and came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.<br>• FIR under old CrPC was <b>Section 154</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – FIR ऑनलाइन और इलेक्ट्रॉनिक संचार के माध्यम से दर्ज की जा सकती है</b><br><b>BNSS, 2023 की धारा 173</b> संज्ञेय अपराध की सूचना <b><u>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक संचार (Electronic communication)</u></b> द्वारा (ई-FIR) देने की अनुमति देती है; सूचनादाता को <b>3 दिनों</b> के भीतर उस पर हस्ताक्षर करने होते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNSS में <b>ज़ीरो FIR</b> का भी प्रावधान है – क्षेत्राधिकार की परवाह किए बिना किसी भी थाने में FIR दर्ज हो सकती है।<br>• BNSS ने <b>CrPC, 1973</b> का स्थान लिया और <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से लागू हुई।<br>• पुरानी CrPC में FIR <b>धारा 154</b> में थी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072616","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Which of the following digital elements are now admissible as primary evidence under the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से डिजिटल तत्व अब प्राथमिक साक्ष्य के रूप में स्वीकार्य हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only CCTV footage","hi":"केवल CCTV फुटेज"},"2":{"en":"Only emails","hi":"केवल ईमेल"},"3":{"en":"Emails, SMS, WhatsApp chats, and cloud data","hi":"ईमेल, SMS, व्हाट्सऐप चैट और क्लाउड डेटा"},"4":{"en":"Only SMS","hi":"केवल SMS"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Emails, SMS, WhatsApp chats, and cloud data</b><br>The <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b> widens \"document\" to include <b>electronic and digital records</b> such as <b><u>emails, SMS, WhatsApp chats and cloud data</u></b>, which can be admitted as primary evidence.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• BSA replaced the <b>Indian Evidence Act, 1872</b>; in force from <b>1 July 2024</b>.<br>• BSA has <b>170 sections</b> (Evidence Act had 167).<br>• The three new criminal laws: <b>BNS</b> (replaced IPC), <b>BNSS</b> (replaced CrPC) and <b>BSA</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ईमेल, SMS, व्हाट्सऐप चैट और क्लाउड डेटा</b><br><b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023</b> \"दस्तावेज़\" की परिभाषा में <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक और डिजिटल अभिलेख</b> जैसे <b><u>ईमेल, SMS, व्हाट्सऐप चैट और क्लाउड डेटा</u></b> को शामिल करता है, जिन्हें प्राथमिक साक्ष्य के रूप में स्वीकार किया जा सकता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BSA ने <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872</b> का स्थान लिया; <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से लागू।<br>• BSA में <b>170 धाराएँ</b> हैं (साक्ष्य अधिनियम में 167 थीं)।<br>• तीन नए आपराधिक कानून: <b>BNS</b> (IPC के स्थान पर), <b>BNSS</b> (CrPC के स्थान पर) और <b>BSA</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072617","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who among the following was the first Indian to win a Grand Slam title? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से ग्रैंड स्लैम खिताब जीतने वाले पहले भारतीय कौन थे? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mahesh Bhupati","hi":"महेश भूपति"},"2":{"en":"Leander Paes","hi":"लिएंडर पेस"},"3":{"en":"Sania Mirza","hi":"सानिया मिर्ज़ा"},"4":{"en":"Rohan Bopanna","hi":"रोहन बोपन्ना"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Mahesh Bhupati</b><br><b><u>Mahesh Bhupathi</u></b> became the first Indian to win a Grand Slam title when he won the <b>1997 French Open mixed doubles</b> with <b>Rika Hiraki</b> of Japan.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bhupathi completed a <b>career Grand Slam in mixed doubles</b>.<br>• <b>Leander Paes</b> won Olympic bronze at <b>Atlanta 1996</b>.<br>• <b>Sania Mirza</b> was the first Indian woman to win a Grand Slam (2009 Australian Open mixed doubles).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – महेश भूपति</b><br><b><u>महेश भूपति</u></b> <b>1997 फ्रेंच ओपन मिश्रित युगल</b> जापान की <b>रिका हिराकी</b> के साथ जीतकर ग्रैंड स्लैम खिताब जीतने वाले पहले भारतीय बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भूपति ने <b>मिश्रित युगल में करियर ग्रैंड स्लैम</b> पूरा किया।<br>• <b>लिएंडर पेस</b> ने <b>अटलांटा 1996</b> ओलंपिक में कांस्य जीता।<br>• <b>सानिया मिर्ज़ा</b> ग्रैंड स्लैम जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला थीं (2009 ऑस्ट्रेलियन ओपन मिश्रित युगल)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072618","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"'Train to Pakistan' is a novel written by which of the following novelists? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"'ट्रेन टू पाकिस्तान' निम्नलिखित में से किस उपन्यासकार द्वारा लिखा गया उपन्यास है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Salman Rushdie","hi":"सलमान रुश्दी"},"2":{"en":"Khushwant Singh","hi":"खुशवंत सिंह"},"3":{"en":"Ismat Chugtai","hi":"इस्मत चुग़ताई"},"4":{"en":"Mulk Raj Anand","hi":"मुल्क राज आनंद"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Khushwant Singh</b><br><b><u>Khushwant Singh</u></b> wrote <b>Train to Pakistan</b> (1956), a novel on the Partition of 1947, set in the fictional border village of <b>Mano Majra</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Other works of Khushwant Singh: <b>Delhi, The Company of Women, Truth, Love and a Little Malice</b> (autobiography).<br>• <b>Mulk Raj Anand</b> – Untouchable, Coolie; <b>Ismat Chughtai</b> – Lihaaf.<br>• Khushwant Singh was awarded the <b>Padma Vibhushan</b> in <b>2007</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – खुशवंत सिंह</b><br><b><u>खुशवंत सिंह</u></b> ने 1947 के विभाजन पर आधारित उपन्यास <b>ट्रेन टू पाकिस्तान</b> (1956) लिखा, जो काल्पनिक सीमावर्ती गाँव <b>मनो माजरा</b> की पृष्ठभूमि पर है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• खुशवंत सिंह की अन्य रचनाएँ: <b>दिल्ली, द कंपनी ऑफ वुमन, ट्रुथ, लव एंड अ लिटिल मैलिस</b> (आत्मकथा)।<br>• <b>मुल्क राज आनंद</b> – अनटचेबल, कुली; <b>इस्मत चुग़ताई</b> – लिहाफ़।<br>• खुशवंत सिंह को <b>2007</b> में <b>पद्म विभूषण</b> मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072619","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Gupta Dynasty","question":{"en":"During which period were the 18 Puranas in their present form composed? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"18 पुराण अपने वर्तमान स्वरूप में किस काल में रचे गए? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mauryan period","hi":"मौर्य काल"},"2":{"en":"Gupta period","hi":"गुप्त काल"},"3":{"en":"Rig Vedic period","hi":"ऋग्वैदिक काल"},"4":{"en":"Vijayanagara period","hi":"विजयनगर काल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Gupta period</b><br>Though older in origin, the <b>Puranas</b> were compiled and given their <b>present form</b> during the <b><u>Gupta period</u></b>, along with the final versions of the Ramayana and Mahabharata.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Puranas are traditionally attributed to <b>Ved Vyasa</b>; the oldest is considered the <b>Matsya Purana</b>.<br>• Puranas deal with five themes (<b>Panchalakshana</b>): creation, re-creation, genealogy, Manvantaras and dynastic history.<br>• The Gupta period is called the <b>\"Golden Age\"</b> of ancient India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – गुप्त काल</b><br>यद्यपि इनका मूल पुराना है, <b>पुराणों</b> को रामायण और महाभारत के अंतिम रूप के साथ <b><u>गुप्त काल</u></b> में संकलित कर <b>वर्तमान स्वरूप</b> दिया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पुराणों को परंपरागत रूप से <b>वेद व्यास</b> से जोड़ा जाता है; सबसे प्राचीन <b>मत्स्य पुराण</b> माना जाता है।<br>• पुराण पाँच विषयों (<b>पंचलक्षण</b>) से संबंधित हैं: सर्ग, प्रतिसर्ग, वंश, मन्वंतर और वंशानुचरित।<br>• गुप्त काल को प्राचीन भारत का <b>\"स्वर्ण युग\"</b> कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072620","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Forest and Grassland","question":{"en":"In India, tropical and subtropical moist broadleaf forests can be found in: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत में उष्णकटिबंधीय और उपोष्णकटिबंधीय नम चौड़ी पत्ती वाले वन कहाँ पाए जा सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Andaman Islands","hi":"अंडमान द्वीप समूह"},"2":{"en":"Brahmaputra Valley","hi":"ब्रह्मपुत्र घाटी"},"3":{"en":"Lower Gangetic Plains","hi":"निचले गंगा के मैदान"},"4":{"en":"All of these","hi":"ये सभी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – All of these</b><br>Tropical and subtropical moist broadleaf forests occur in areas of high rainfall and humidity – the <b>Andaman Islands</b>, <b>Brahmaputra Valley</b>, <b>Lower Gangetic Plains</b>, Western Ghats and North-East. Hence <b><u>All of these</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Tropical evergreen forests need rainfall of more than <b>200 cm</b>; trees include <b>ebony, mahogany, rosewood</b>.<br>• <b>Tropical deciduous (monsoon) forests</b> are the most widespread forests in India.<br>• As per ISFR 2023, forest and tree cover together form about <b>25%</b> of India's area.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – ये सभी</b><br>उष्णकटिबंधीय और उपोष्णकटिबंधीय नम चौड़ी पत्ती वाले वन अधिक वर्षा और आर्द्रता वाले क्षेत्रों – <b>अंडमान द्वीप</b>, <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र घाटी</b>, <b>निचले गंगा के मैदान</b>, पश्चिमी घाट और पूर्वोत्तर में पाए जाते हैं। अतः <b><u>ये सभी</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उष्णकटिबंधीय सदाबहार वनों के लिए <b>200 cm</b> से अधिक वर्षा चाहिए; वृक्ष – <b>आबनूस, महोगनी, रोज़वुड</b>।<br>• <b>उष्णकटिबंधीय पर्णपाती (मानसूनी) वन</b> भारत में सबसे विस्तृत वन हैं।<br>• ISFR 2023 के अनुसार वन और वृक्ष आवरण मिलकर भारत के क्षेत्रफल का लगभग <b>25%</b> हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072621","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Read the following three statements related to the festivals of Mizoram:<br>1) Mim Kut is held in August and September, after the maize harvest.<br>2) Chapchar Kut in spring includes night-long dancing after jhum cutting.<br>3) Pawl Kut features drinking of rice beer during the festival.<br>Which of the above statements is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मिज़ोरम के त्योहारों से संबंधित निम्नलिखित तीन कथनों को पढ़िए:<br>1) मिम कुट अगस्त और सितंबर में मक्के की फसल के बाद मनाया जाता है।<br>2) वसंत में मनाए जाने वाले चापचार कुट में झूम कटाई के बाद रात भर नृत्य होता है।<br>3) पॉल कुट में त्योहार के दौरान चावल की बीयर पी जाती है।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1 is correct","hi":"केवल 1 सही है"},"2":{"en":"Only 2 is correct","hi":"केवल 2 सही है"},"3":{"en":"Only 3 is correct","hi":"केवल 3 सही है"},"4":{"en":"1, 2 and 3 are correct","hi":"1, 2 और 3 सही हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 1, 2 and 3 are correct</b><br>The three Kuts of Mizoram are agricultural festivals: <b>Mim Kut</b> (Aug–Sept, after maize harvest), <b>Chapchar Kut</b> (spring, after clearing jhum land, with dances) and <b>Pawl Kut</b> (harvest festival with feasting and rice beer). All are correct: <b><u>1, 2 and 3</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Cheraw (Bamboo Dance)</b> is the famous dance of Mizoram, performed during Chapchar Kut.<br>• Pawl Kut is celebrated in <b>December–January</b> after the paddy harvest.<br>• \"Kut\" means <b>festival</b> in the Mizo language.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 1, 2 और 3 सही हैं</b><br>मिज़ोरम के तीनों कुट कृषि त्योहार हैं: <b>मिम कुट</b> (अगस्त–सितंबर, मक्का कटाई के बाद), <b>चापचार कुट</b> (वसंत, झूम भूमि साफ करने के बाद, नृत्य सहित) और <b>पॉल कुट</b> (भोज और चावल की बीयर के साथ फसल उत्सव)। सभी सही हैं: <b><u>1, 2 और 3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>चेराव (बाँस नृत्य)</b> मिज़ोरम का प्रसिद्ध नृत्य है, जो चापचार कुट में किया जाता है।<br>• पॉल कुट धान की कटाई के बाद <b>दिसंबर–जनवरी</b> में मनाया जाता है।<br>• मिज़ो भाषा में \"कुट\" का अर्थ <b>त्योहार</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072622","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"At the Paris Olympics 2024, which Indian female shooter won an Olympic medal in the 10m Air Pistol event, becoming the first-ever woman from India to do so? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"पेरिस ओलंपिक 2024 में किस भारतीय महिला निशानेबाज़ ने 10 मीटर एयर पिस्टल स्पर्धा में ओलंपिक पदक जीतकर ऐसा करने वाली पहली भारतीय महिला बनने का गौरव प्राप्त किया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Esha Singh","hi":"ईशा सिंह"},"2":{"en":"Manu Bhaker","hi":"मनु भाकर"},"3":{"en":"Apurvi Chandela","hi":"अपूर्वी चंदेला"},"4":{"en":"Anjali Bhagwat","hi":"अंजलि भागवत"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Manu Bhaker</b><br><b><u>Manu Bhaker</u></b> won <b>bronze</b> in the women's 10m Air Pistol at Paris 2024, becoming India's <b>first woman shooter to win an Olympic medal</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She also won bronze in <b>10m Air Pistol mixed team</b> with <b>Sarabjot Singh</b> – first Indian since Independence to win <b>two medals at one Olympics</b>.<br>• India won <b>6 medals</b> at Paris 2024 (1 silver, 5 bronze).<br>• Manu Bhaker received the <b>Major Dhyan Chand Khel Ratna</b> in 2025.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – मनु भाकर</b><br><b><u>मनु भाकर</u></b> ने पेरिस 2024 में महिला 10 मीटर एयर पिस्टल में <b>कांस्य</b> जीता और ओलंपिक पदक जीतने वाली <b>पहली भारतीय महिला निशानेबाज़</b> बनीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्होंने <b>सरबजोत सिंह</b> के साथ <b>10 मीटर एयर पिस्टल मिश्रित टीम</b> में भी कांस्य जीता – स्वतंत्रता के बाद <b>एक ओलंपिक में दो पदक</b> जीतने वाली पहली भारतीय।<br>• पेरिस 2024 में भारत ने <b>6 पदक</b> जीते (1 रजत, 5 कांस्य)।<br>• मनु भाकर को 2025 में <b>मेजर ध्यानचंद खेल रत्न</b> मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072623","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Transport","question":{"en":"Which of the following ports on India’s eastern coastline is best known for exporting iron ore and coal, due to its location near the mineral-rich areas of Odisha and Chhattisgarh? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के पूर्वी तट पर स्थित निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा बंदरगाह ओडिशा और छत्तीसगढ़ के खनिज-समृद्ध क्षेत्रों के निकट होने के कारण लौह अयस्क और कोयले के निर्यात के लिए सबसे अधिक जाना जाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Chennai Port","hi":"चेन्नई बंदरगाह"},"2":{"en":"Paradip Port","hi":"पारादीप बंदरगाह"},"3":{"en":"Visakhapatnam Port","hi":"विशाखापत्तनम बंदरगाह"},"4":{"en":"Kolkata Port","hi":"कोलकाता बंदरगाह"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Paradip Port</b><br><b><u>Paradip Port</u></b> in Odisha, at the confluence of the Mahanadi and the Bay of Bengal, mainly handles <b>iron ore, coal and other minerals</b> from Odisha, Jharkhand and Chhattisgarh.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Paradip was commissioned in <b>1966</b> as the first major port on the east coast after Independence.<br>• <b>Visakhapatnam</b> is the deepest land-locked and protected port; exports iron ore from <b>Bailadila</b> to Japan.<br>• <b>Kolkata (Syama Prasad Mookerjee Port)</b> is India's only major <b>riverine port</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पारादीप बंदरगाह</b><br>ओडिशा में महानदी और बंगाल की खाड़ी के संगम पर स्थित <b><u>पारादीप बंदरगाह</u></b> मुख्यतः ओडिशा, झारखंड और छत्तीसगढ़ के <b>लौह अयस्क, कोयले और अन्य खनिजों</b> का संचालन करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पारादीप <b>1966</b> में स्वतंत्रता के बाद पूर्वी तट के पहले प्रमुख बंदरगाह के रूप में शुरू हुआ।<br>• <b>विशाखापत्तनम</b> सबसे गहरा भू-आबद्ध और संरक्षित बंदरगाह है; <b>बैलाडीला</b> का लौह अयस्क जापान भेजता है।<br>• <b>कोलकाता (श्यामा प्रसाद मुखर्जी बंदरगाह)</b> भारत का एकमात्र प्रमुख <b>नदी बंदरगाह</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072624","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which of the following districts in Assam are known for having major oil wells? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"असम के निम्नलिखित में से कौन-से ज़िले प्रमुख तेल कुओं के लिए जाने जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dibrugarh and Jorhat","hi":"डिब्रूगढ़ और जोरहाट"},"2":{"en":"Digboi and Naharkatiya","hi":"डिगबोई और नहरकटिया"},"3":{"en":"Guwahati and Tezpur","hi":"गुवाहाटी और तेज़पुर"},"4":{"en":"Nagaon and Barpeta","hi":"नगाँव और बारपेटा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Digboi and Naharkatiya</b><br><b><u>Digboi and Naharkatiya</u></b> (along with Moran) are the main oil fields of Upper Assam. Digboi is the site of Asia's oldest oil well.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Digboi refinery (1901)</b> is the oldest operating refinery in Asia.<br>• India's first oil was struck at <b>Makum (Assam) in 1867</b>.<br>• <b>Mumbai High</b> is India's largest offshore oil field; <b>Ankleshwar</b> is a major field in Gujarat.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – डिगबोई और नहरकटिया</b><br><b><u>डिगबोई और नहरकटिया</u></b> (मोरान सहित) ऊपरी असम के प्रमुख तेल क्षेत्र हैं। डिगबोई में एशिया का सबसे पुराना तेल कुआँ है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>डिगबोई रिफाइनरी (1901)</b> एशिया की सबसे पुरानी चालू रिफाइनरी है।<br>• भारत में पहली बार तेल <b>1867 में माकुम (असम)</b> में मिला।<br>• <b>मुंबई हाई</b> भारत का सबसे बड़ा अपतटीय तेल क्षेत्र है; <b>अंकलेश्वर</b> गुजरात का प्रमुख क्षेत्र है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072625","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Article 131A was repealed and previously gave exclusive jurisdiction to _____. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"अनुच्छेद 131A निरसित कर दिया गया था और पहले यह _____ को अनन्य क्षेत्राधिकार देता था। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"District Courts","hi":"ज़िला न्यायालयों"},"2":{"en":"High Courts","hi":"उच्च न्यायालयों"},"3":{"en":"Supreme Court","hi":"सर्वोच्च न्यायालय"},"4":{"en":"Election Commission","hi":"निर्वाचन आयोग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Supreme Court</b><br><b>Article 131A</b>, inserted by the <b>42<sup>nd</sup> Amendment (1976)</b>, gave the <b><u>Supreme Court</u></b> exclusive jurisdiction over questions on the constitutional validity of central laws. It was repealed by the <b>43<sup>rd</sup> Amendment (1977)</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 131</b> – original jurisdiction of the Supreme Court in Centre–State and inter-State disputes.<br>• <b>Article 32</b> – writ jurisdiction; <b>Article 136</b> – Special Leave Petition.<br>• The 42<sup>nd</sup> Amendment is called the <b>\"Mini Constitution\"</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय</b><br><b>42वें संशोधन (1976)</b> द्वारा जोड़ा गया <b>अनुच्छेद 131A</b> केंद्रीय कानूनों की संवैधानिक वैधता के प्रश्नों पर <b><u>सर्वोच्च न्यायालय</u></b> को अनन्य क्षेत्राधिकार देता था। इसे <b>43वें संशोधन (1977)</b> द्वारा निरसित किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 131</b> – केंद्र–राज्य और अंतर-राज्यीय विवादों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का मूल क्षेत्राधिकार।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 32</b> – रिट क्षेत्राधिकार; <b>अनुच्छेद 136</b> – विशेष अनुमति याचिका (SLP)।<br>• 42वें संशोधन को <b>\"लघु संविधान (Mini Constitution)\"</b> कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072626","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Local Government","question":{"en":"Under which Constitutional Amendment Act was Article 243ZD, relating to the Committee for District Planning, inserted into the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"ज़िला योजना समिति से संबंधित अनुच्छेद 243ZD किस संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम द्वारा भारतीय संविधान में जोड़ा गया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The 72<sup>nd</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992","hi":"72वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992"},"2":{"en":"The 73<sup>rd</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992","hi":"73वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992"},"3":{"en":"The 74<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992","hi":"74वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992"},"4":{"en":"The 75<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1993","hi":"75वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1993"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The 74<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992</b><br>The <b><u>74<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992</u></b> added <b>Part IXA (Municipalities)</b>, Articles 243P–243ZG, including <b>Article 243ZD</b> on the <b>District Planning Committee</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 74<sup>th</sup> Amendment also added the <b>12<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b> with <b>18 subjects</b>.<br>• <b>Article 243ZE</b> – Metropolitan Planning Committee.<br>• The <b>73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment</b> added Part IX (Panchayats) and the 11<sup>th</sup> Schedule (29 subjects).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 74वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992</b><br><b><u>74वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992</u></b> ने <b>भाग IXA (नगरपालिकाएँ)</b>, अनुच्छेद 243P–243ZG जोड़े, जिनमें <b>ज़िला योजना समिति</b> से संबंधित <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZD</b> शामिल है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 74वें संशोधन ने <b>18 विषयों</b> वाली <b>12वीं अनुसूची</b> भी जोड़ी।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZE</b> – महानगर योजना समिति।<br>• <b>73वें संशोधन</b> ने भाग IX (पंचायतें) और 11वीं अनुसूची (29 विषय) जोड़ी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072627","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Under which Constitutional Amendment Act was Article 243ZI, concerning the incorporation of co-operative societies, inserted into the Indian Constitution? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सहकारी समितियों के निगमन से संबंधित अनुच्छेद 243ZI किस संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम द्वारा भारतीय संविधान में जोड़ा गया? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The 74<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992","hi":"74वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992"},"2":{"en":"The 91<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2003","hi":"91वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2003"},"3":{"en":"The 97<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2011","hi":"97वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2011"},"4":{"en":"The 101<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016","hi":"101वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The 97<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2011</b><br>The <b><u>97<sup>th</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2011</u></b> added <b>Part IXB (Co-operative Societies)</b>, Articles 243ZH–243ZT; <b>Article 243ZI</b> deals with their incorporation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It also made forming co-operative societies a <b>Fundamental Right under Article 19(1)(c)</b> and added <b>Article 43B</b> (DPSP).<br>• In <b>2021</b>, the Supreme Court struck down parts of Part IXB relating to state co-operatives.<br>• <b>91<sup>st</sup> Amendment</b> – limited Council of Ministers to 15% of the House; <b>101<sup>st</sup></b> – GST.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 97वाँ संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2011</b><br><b><u>97वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2011</u></b> ने <b>भाग IXB (सहकारी समितियाँ)</b>, अनुच्छेद 243ZH–243ZT जोड़े; <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZI</b> उनके निगमन से संबंधित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने सहकारी समितियाँ बनाने को <b>अनुच्छेद 19(1)(c) के तहत मौलिक अधिकार</b> बनाया और <b>अनुच्छेद 43B</b> (DPSP) जोड़ा।<br>• <b>2021</b> में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने राज्य सहकारी समितियों से संबंधित भाग IXB के अंशों को निरस्त किया।<br>• <b>91वाँ संशोधन</b> – मंत्रिपरिषद को सदन के 15% तक सीमित किया; <b>101वाँ</b> – GST।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072628","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Part 1 and Part 2 of the Constitution","question":{"en":"In the Constitution of India, what does the phrase “Union of States” signify? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"भारत के संविधान में “राज्यों का संघ” वाक्यांश क्या दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India follows a presidential form of government.","hi":"भारत में राष्ट्रपति शासन प्रणाली है।"},"2":{"en":"Complete unitary system.","hi":"पूर्णतः एकात्मक व्यवस्था।"},"3":{"en":"States created the Union.","hi":"राज्यों ने संघ का निर्माण किया।"},"4":{"en":"Federation is not the result of an agreement among states.","hi":"संघ राज्यों के बीच किसी समझौते का परिणाम नहीं है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Federation is not the result of an agreement among states.</b><br>Dr. Ambedkar explained that \"Union of States\" (Article 1) means the Indian federation is <b><u>not the result of an agreement among the states</u></b>, and therefore no state has the right to <b>secede</b> from it.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 1</b>: \"India, that is Bharat, shall be a Union of States.\"<br>• The Indian federation is called <b>\"indestructible Union of destructible States\"</b>; Parliament can alter state boundaries under <b>Article 3</b>.<br>• Unlike India, the <b>USA</b> federation was formed by an agreement among states.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – संघ राज्यों के बीच किसी समझौते का परिणाम नहीं है।</b><br>डॉ. अंबेडकर ने स्पष्ट किया कि \"राज्यों का संघ\" (अनुच्छेद 1) का अर्थ है कि भारतीय संघ <b><u>राज्यों के बीच किसी समझौते का परिणाम नहीं है</u></b>, इसलिए किसी राज्य को इससे <b>अलग होने (Secede)</b> का अधिकार नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 1</b>: \"भारत, अर्थात् इंडिया, राज्यों का संघ होगा।\"<br>• भारतीय संघ को <b>\"विनाशी राज्यों का अविनाशी संघ\"</b> कहा जाता है; संसद <b>अनुच्छेद 3</b> के तहत राज्यों की सीमाएँ बदल सकती है।<br>• भारत के विपरीत, <b>अमेरिका</b> का संघ राज्यों के बीच समझौते से बना।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072629","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which of the following constitutes foreign investment in India after the introduction of the New Economic Policy (1991)? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"नई आर्थिक नीति (1991) लागू होने के बाद भारत में विदेशी निवेश में निम्नलिखित में से क्या शामिल है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Foreign Institutional Investment and Bilateral Development Finance","hi":"विदेशी संस्थागत निवेश और द्विपक्षीय विकास वित्त"},"2":{"en":"Foreign Direct Investment and Official Development Assistance","hi":"प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश और आधिकारिक विकास सहायता"},"3":{"en":"Foreign Portfolio Investment and External Commercial Borrowings","hi":"विदेशी पोर्टफोलियो निवेश और बाह्य वाणिज्यिक उधार"},"4":{"en":"Foreign Direct Investment and Foreign Institutional Investment","hi":"प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश और विदेशी संस्थागत निवेश"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Foreign Direct Investment and Foreign Institutional Investment</b><br>As per NCERT, foreign investment after 1991 includes <b><u>Foreign Direct Investment (FDI)</u></b> and <b><u>Foreign Institutional Investment (FII)</u></b>. Aid and borrowings are debt flows, not investment.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>FDI</b> gives a lasting interest and control (generally 10% or more equity); <b>FII/FPI</b> is investment in shares and bonds.<br>• FDI in India is regulated under <b>FEMA, 1999</b>.<br>• FII has been renamed <b>Foreign Portfolio Investment (FPI)</b>, regulated by <b>SEBI</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश और विदेशी संस्थागत निवेश</b><br>NCERT के अनुसार 1991 के बाद विदेशी निवेश में <b><u>प्रत्यक्ष विदेशी निवेश (FDI)</u></b> और <b><u>विदेशी संस्थागत निवेश (FII)</u></b> शामिल हैं। सहायता और उधार ऋण प्रवाह हैं, निवेश नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>FDI</b> में स्थायी हित और नियंत्रण होता है (सामान्यतः 10% या अधिक इक्विटी); <b>FII/FPI</b> शेयरों और बॉन्ड में निवेश है।<br>• भारत में FDI <b>FEMA, 1999</b> के तहत विनियमित है।<br>• FII का नाम बदलकर <b>विदेशी पोर्टफोलियो निवेश (FPI)</b> किया गया, जिसे <b>SEBI</b> विनियमित करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072630","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Radioactivity","question":{"en":"The half-life of a radionuclide is 4 hours. If its initial mass is 160 g (gram), what mass of the radionuclide will remain undecayed after 12 hours? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"किसी रेडियोन्यूक्लाइड की अर्ध-आयु 4 घंटे है। यदि इसका प्रारंभिक द्रव्यमान 160 g (ग्राम) है, तो 12 घंटे बाद कितना द्रव्यमान अविघटित रहेगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20 (gram)","hi":"20 (ग्राम)"},"2":{"en":"40 (gram)","hi":"40 (ग्राम)"},"3":{"en":"80 (gram)","hi":"80 (ग्राम)"},"4":{"en":"10 (gram)","hi":"10 (ग्राम)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 20 (gram)</b><br>Number of half-lives \\(n = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\\)<br>\\(m = m_0 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n = 160 \\times \\frac{1}{8} = 20\\) g<br>(160 → 80 → 40 → <b><u>20 g</u></b>)<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Half-life \\(T_{1/2} = \\frac{0.693}{\\lambda}\\), where λ is the decay constant.<br>• Half-life does not depend on temperature, pressure or initial amount.<br>• Radioactivity was discovered by <b>Henri Becquerel (1896)</b>; SI unit is the <b>becquerel (Bq)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 20 (ग्राम)</b><br>अर्ध-आयुओं की संख्या \\(n = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\\)<br>\\(m = m_0 \\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^n = 160 \\times \\frac{1}{8} = 20\\) g<br>(160 → 80 → 40 → <b><u>20 g</u></b>)<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अर्ध-आयु \\(T_{1/2} = \\frac{0.693}{\\lambda}\\), जहाँ λ क्षय नियतांक (Decay constant) है।<br>• अर्ध-आयु ताप, दाब या प्रारंभिक मात्रा पर निर्भर नहीं करती।<br>• रेडियोधर्मिता की खोज <b>हेनरी बेकरल (1896)</b> ने की; SI मात्रक <b>बेकरल (Bq)</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072631","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hemispherical bowl is made of steel, 1 cm thick. The inner radius of the bowl is 4 cm. What will be the outer curved surface area? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अर्धगोलाकार कटोरा स्टील का बना है, जिसकी मोटाई 1 cm है। कटोरे की आंतरिक त्रिज्या 4 cm है। बाहरी वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"137.14 cm²"},"2":{"en":"237.14 cm²"},"3":{"en":"257.14 cm²"},"4":{"en":"157.14 cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Outer radius \\(= 4 + 1 = 5\\) cm<br>Outer curved surface area \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 25\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1100}{7} = \\boxed{157.14\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 157.14 cm².</b>","hi":"बाहरी त्रिज्या \\(= 4 + 1 = 5\\) cm<br>बाहरी वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 25\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1100}{7} = \\boxed{157.14\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 157.14 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072632","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If all edges of a rectangular parallelepiped are equal, it becomes a: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि किसी आयताकार समांतर षट्फलक के सभी किनारे बराबर हों, तो वह बन जाता है: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Sphere","hi":"गोला"},"2":{"en":"Cube","hi":"घन"},"3":{"en":"Cylinder","hi":"बेलन"},"4":{"en":"Cone","hi":"शंकु"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A rectangular parallelepiped has length, breadth and height \\(l, b, h\\)<br>If \\(l = b = h\\), all faces become equal squares<br>Such a solid is a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Cube}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Cube.</b>","hi":"आयताकार समांतर षट्फलक की लंबाई, चौड़ाई और ऊँचाई \\(l, b, h\\) होती हैं<br>यदि \\(l = b = h\\), तो सभी फलक बराबर वर्ग बन जाते हैं<br>ऐसा ठोस \\(\\boxed{\\text{घन}}\\) होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): घन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072633","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If a * b = a + b + ab, then 3 * 5 - 2 * 4 is equal to? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि a * b = a + b + ab है, तो 3 * 5 - 2 * 4 किसके बराबर है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"13"},"4":{"en":"23"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(3 * 5 = 3 + 5 + 15 = 23\\)<br>\\(2 * 4 = 2 + 4 + 8 = 14\\)<br>\\(23 - 14 = \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 9.</b>","hi":"\\(3 * 5 = 3 + 5 + 15 = 23\\)<br>\\(2 * 4 = 2 + 4 + 8 = 14\\)<br>\\(23 - 14 = \\boxed{9}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072634","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The sides of a triangle are 7 cm, 24 cm, and 25 cm. What is the length of the altitude corresponding to the longest side? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक त्रिभुज की भुजाएँ 7 cm, 24 cm और 25 cm हैं। सबसे बड़ी भुजा पर डाले गए लंब की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5.6 cm"},"2":{"en":"6.72 cm"},"3":{"en":"8.4 cm"},"4":{"en":"9.6 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Since \\(7^2 + 24^2 = 25^2\\), it is a right triangle with legs 7 and 24<br>Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 7 \\times 24 = 84\\) cm²<br>Altitude on the longest side \\(= \\frac{2 \\times 84}{25} = \\boxed{6.72\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6.72 cm.</b>","hi":"चूँकि \\(7^2 + 24^2 = 25^2\\), यह 7 और 24 भुजाओं वाला समकोण त्रिभुज है<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 7 \\times 24 = 84\\) cm²<br>सबसे बड़ी भुजा पर लंब \\(= \\frac{2 \\times 84}{25} = \\boxed{6.72\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6.72 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072635","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two complementary angles add up to 90°. If one angle is 18° less than the other, find the angles. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो पूरक कोणों का योग 90° होता है। यदि एक कोण दूसरे से 18° कम है, तो कोण ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36°, 54°"},"2":{"en":"28°, 62°"},"3":{"en":"40°, 50°"},"4":{"en":"45°, 45°"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Let the angles be \\(x\\) and \\(x - 18°\\)<br>\\(x + x - 18° = 90° \\Rightarrow 2x = 108° \\Rightarrow x = 54°\\)<br>Angles \\(= \\boxed{36°, 54°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 36°, 54°.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए कोण \\(x\\) और \\(x - 18°\\) हैं<br>\\(x + x - 18° = 90° \\Rightarrow 2x = 108° \\Rightarrow x = 54°\\)<br>कोण \\(= \\boxed{36°, 54°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 36°, 54° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072636","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The heights of two cones are in the ratio 1:3, and the radii of their bases are in the ratio 3:1. What is the ratio of their volumes? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो शंकुओं की ऊँचाइयाँ 1:3 के अनुपात में हैं और उनके आधारों की त्रिज्याएँ 3:1 के अनुपात में हैं। उनके आयतनों का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3 : 4"},"2":{"en":"4 : 3"},"3":{"en":"3 : 1"},"4":{"en":"2 : 3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Volume \\(\\propto r^2 h\\)<br>Ratio \\(= \\frac{3^2 \\times 1}{1^2 \\times 3} = \\frac{9}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3 : 1.</b>","hi":"आयतन \\(\\propto r^2 h\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= \\frac{3^2 \\times 1}{1^2 \\times 3} = \\frac{9}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 : 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072637","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hemispherical brass bowl has an inner diameter of 28 cm. If the inside of the bowl is to be painted at the rate of ₹30 per cm², what will be the total cost of painting the inner curved surface? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक अर्धगोलाकार पीतल के कटोरे का आंतरिक व्यास 28 cm है। यदि कटोरे के भीतरी भाग को ₹30 प्रति cm² की दर से पेंट किया जाना है, तो आंतरिक वक्र पृष्ठ को पेंट करने की कुल लागत क्या होगी? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹39960"},"2":{"en":"₹36960"},"3":{"en":"₹26960"},"4":{"en":"₹46520"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Inner radius \\(= 14\\) cm<br>Inner curved surface \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 196 = 1232\\) cm²<br>Cost ₹\\(= 1232 \\times 30 = \\boxed{36{,}960}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹36960.</b>","hi":"आंतरिक त्रिज्या \\(= 14\\) cm<br>आंतरिक वक्र पृष्ठ \\(= 2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 196 = 1232\\) cm²<br>लागत ₹\\(= 1232 \\times 30 = \\boxed{36{,}960}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹36960 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072638","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Rita travels a certain fixed distance at her usual speed. If she reduces her speed by 10 km/h, she takes 40 hours more than the original time to complete the journey. On the other hand, if she increases her speed by 15 km/h, she takes 10 hours less than the original time.<br>Find the distance travelled by Rita. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"रीता एक निश्चित दूरी अपनी सामान्य चाल से तय करती है। यदि वह अपनी चाल 10 km/घंटा कम कर दे, तो उसे यात्रा पूरी करने में मूल समय से 40 घंटे अधिक लगते हैं। दूसरी ओर, यदि वह चाल 15 km/घंटा बढ़ा दे, तो उसे मूल समय से 10 घंटे कम लगते हैं।<br>रीता द्वारा तय की गई दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"150 km"},"2":{"en":"250 km"},"3":{"en":"300 km"},"4":{"en":"380 km"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Let the usual speed be \\(v\\) and the distance be \\(D\\)<br>\\(\\frac{D}{v - 10} - \\frac{D}{v} = 40 \\Rightarrow D = 4v(v - 10)\\)<br>\\(\\frac{D}{v} - \\frac{D}{v + 15} = 10 \\Rightarrow D = \\frac{2}{3}v(v + 15)\\)<br>\\(4v(v - 10) = \\frac{2}{3}v(v + 15) \\Rightarrow 12(v - 10) = 2(v + 15) \\Rightarrow 10v = 150 \\Rightarrow v = 15\\)<br>\\(D = 4 \\times 15 \\times 5 = \\boxed{300\\ \\text{km}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 300 km.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए सामान्य चाल \\(v\\) और दूरी \\(D\\) है<br>\\(\\frac{D}{v - 10} - \\frac{D}{v} = 40 \\Rightarrow D = 4v(v - 10)\\)<br>\\(\\frac{D}{v} - \\frac{D}{v + 15} = 10 \\Rightarrow D = \\frac{2}{3}v(v + 15)\\)<br>\\(4v(v - 10) = \\frac{2}{3}v(v + 15) \\Rightarrow 12(v - 10) = 2(v + 15) \\Rightarrow 10v = 150 \\Rightarrow v = 15\\)<br>\\(D = 4 \\times 15 \\times 5 = \\boxed{300\\ \\text{km}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 300 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072639","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Simplify: \\(\\frac{0.05 \\times 0.05 \\times 0.05 + 0.04 \\times 0.04 \\times 0.04}{0.05 \\times 0.05 - 0.05 \\times 0.04 + 0.04 \\times 0.04}\\). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"सरलीकृत कीजिए: \\(\\frac{0.05 \\times 0.05 \\times 0.05 + 0.04 \\times 0.04 \\times 0.04}{0.05 \\times 0.05 - 0.05 \\times 0.04 + 0.04 \\times 0.04}\\) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.07"},"2":{"en":"0.09"},"3":{"en":"0.08"},"4":{"en":"0.05"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{a^3 + b^3}{a^2 - ab + b^2} = a + b\\) with \\(a = 0.05, b = 0.04\\)<br>\\(= 0.05 + 0.04\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.09}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.09.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{a^3 + b^3}{a^2 - ab + b^2} = a + b\\), जहाँ \\(a = 0.05, b = 0.04\\)<br>\\(= 0.05 + 0.04\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{0.09}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.09 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072640","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"The value of \\(\\sqrt{0.09} + \\sqrt{0.49} + \\sqrt{1.21} + \\sqrt{0.0004}\\) is: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{0.09} + \\sqrt{0.49} + \\sqrt{1.21} + \\sqrt{0.0004}\\) का मान है: [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.84"},"2":{"en":"4.06"},"3":{"en":"3.26"},"4":{"en":"2.12"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{0.09} = 0.3\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.49} = 0.7\\), \\(\\sqrt{1.21} = 1.1\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0004} = 0.02\\)<br>Sum \\(= 0.3 + 0.7 + 1.1 + 0.02\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2.12}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2.12.</b>","hi":"\\(\\sqrt{0.09} = 0.3\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.49} = 0.7\\), \\(\\sqrt{1.21} = 1.1\\), \\(\\sqrt{0.0004} = 0.02\\)<br>योग \\(= 0.3 + 0.7 + 1.1 + 0.02\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2.12}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2.12 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072641","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Ram covered the same distance at the speed of 40 km/hr, 45 km/hr and 60 km/hr. What was the average speed of Ram during the whole journey? (Correct to two decimal places.) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"राम ने समान दूरी 40 km/घंटा, 45 km/घंटा और 60 km/घंटा की चाल से तय की। पूरी यात्रा में राम की औसत चाल क्या थी? (दो दशमलव स्थानों तक) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"34.87 km/h"},"2":{"en":"42.80 km/h"},"3":{"en":"38.96 km/h"},"4":{"en":"46.96 km/h"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For equal distances the average speed is the harmonic mean<br>\\(= \\frac{3}{\\frac{1}{40} + \\frac{1}{45} + \\frac{1}{60}} = \\frac{3 \\times 360}{9 + 8 + 6}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1080}{23} = 46.9565 \\approx \\boxed{46.96\\ \\text{km/h}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 46.96 km/h.</b>","hi":"समान दूरियों के लिए औसत चाल हरात्मक माध्य होती है<br>\\(= \\frac{3}{\\frac{1}{40} + \\frac{1}{45} + \\frac{1}{60}} = \\frac{3 \\times 360}{9 + 8 + 6}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1080}{23} = 46.9565 \\approx \\boxed{46.96\\ \\text{km/h}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 46.96 km/h है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072642","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate: \\(\\left[\\frac{(2.7)^3 - (1.3)^3}{(2.7)^2 + 3.51 + (1.3)^2}\\right]^2\\) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(\\left[\\frac{(2.7)^3 - (1.3)^3}{(2.7)^2 + 3.51 + (1.3)^2}\\right]^2\\) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.54"},"2":{"en":"1.96"},"3":{"en":"2.34"},"4":{"en":"2.87"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Here \\(3.51 = 2.7 \\times 1.3\\), so the bracket is \\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 2.7 - 1.3 = 1.4\\)<br>\\((1.4)^2 = \\boxed{1.96}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.96.</b>","hi":"यहाँ \\(3.51 = 2.7 \\times 1.3\\), अतः कोष्ठक \\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\) है<br>\\(= 2.7 - 1.3 = 1.4\\)<br>\\((1.4)^2 = \\boxed{1.96}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1.96 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072643","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △XYZ, let M be the midpoint of side XY. If the length of the median ZM is 9 cm and G is the centroid, what is the length of segment GM? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"△XYZ में, मान लीजिए M भुजा XY का मध्यबिंदु है। यदि माध्यिका ZM की लंबाई 9 cm है और G केन्द्रक है, तो खंड GM की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 cm"},"2":{"en":"7 cm"},"3":{"en":"9 cm"},"4":{"en":"3 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The centroid divides the median in the ratio 2 : 1 from the vertex<br>\\(GM = \\frac{1}{3} \\times ZM = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 9\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3 cm.</b>","hi":"केन्द्रक माध्यिका को शीर्ष से 2 : 1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है<br>\\(GM = \\frac{1}{3} \\times ZM = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 9\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072644","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Two workers A and B working together completed a job in 8 days. If A had worked with twice efficiency as he actually did, B had worked with 60% of efficiency as he actually did. The work would have been completed in 6 days. To complete the job alone, B would require how many days? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो कार्मिक A और B ने मिलकर एक कार्य 8 दिनों में पूरा किया। यदि A अपनी वास्तविक कार्यक्षमता की दोगुनी क्षमता से और B अपनी वास्तविक कार्यक्षमता के 60% से कार्य करता, तो कार्य 6 दिनों में पूरा हो जाता। अकेले कार्य पूरा करने में B को कितने दिन लगेंगे? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(14\\frac{3}{5}\\) days","hi":"\\(14\\frac{3}{5}\\) दिन"},"2":{"en":"\\(16\\frac{4}{5}\\) days","hi":"\\(16\\frac{4}{5}\\) दिन"},"3":{"en":"\\(13\\frac{2}{5}\\) days","hi":"\\(13\\frac{2}{5}\\) दिन"},"4":{"en":"\\(18\\frac{1}{5}\\) days","hi":"\\(18\\frac{1}{5}\\) दिन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Let A's one-day work be \\(a\\) and B's be \\(b\\)<br>\\(8a + 8b = 1\\) and \\(6(2a) + 6(0.6b) = 1\\)<br>\\(12a + 3.6b = 1\\) and \\(a = \\frac{1 - 8b}{8}\\)<br>\\(12\\left(\\frac{1 - 8b}{8}\\right) + 3.6b = 1 \\Rightarrow 1.5 - 12b + 3.6b = 1 \\Rightarrow 8.4b = 0.5\\)<br>\\(b = \\frac{0.5}{8.4} = \\frac{1}{16.8}\\), so B alone takes \\(16.8\\) days \\(= \\boxed{16\\frac{4}{5}\\ \\text{days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(16\\frac{4}{5}\\) days.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए A का एक-दिन का कार्य \\(a\\) और B का \\(b\\) है<br>\\(8a + 8b = 1\\) और \\(6(2a) + 6(0.6b) = 1\\)<br>\\(12a + 3.6b = 1\\) तथा \\(a = \\frac{1 - 8b}{8}\\)<br>\\(12\\left(\\frac{1 - 8b}{8}\\right) + 3.6b = 1 \\Rightarrow 1.5 - 12b + 3.6b = 1 \\Rightarrow 8.4b = 0.5\\)<br>\\(b = \\frac{0.5}{8.4} = \\frac{1}{16.8}\\), अतः B अकेले \\(16.8\\) दिन \\(= \\boxed{16\\frac{4}{5}\\ \\text{दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(16\\frac{4}{5}\\) दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072645","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Which of the following numbers is NOT divisible by 3? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी संख्या 3 से विभाज्य नहीं है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"98763"},"2":{"en":"10002"},"3":{"en":"55554"},"4":{"en":"71203"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Check the digit sums: \\(9+8+7+6+3 = 33\\), \\(1+0+0+0+2 = 3\\), \\(5+5+5+5+4 = 24\\)<br>All are multiples of 3, while \\(7+1+2+0+3 = 13\\)<br>So \\(\\boxed{71203}\\) is not divisible by 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 71203.</b>","hi":"अंकों के योग देखिए: \\(9+8+7+6+3 = 33\\), \\(1+0+0+0+2 = 3\\), \\(5+5+5+5+4 = 24\\)<br>ये सभी 3 के गुणज हैं, जबकि \\(7+1+2+0+3 = 13\\)<br>अतः \\(\\boxed{71203}\\), 3 से विभाज्य नहीं है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 71203 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072646","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"How many numbers from 50 to 1000 are divisible by 11? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"50 से 1000 तक कितनी संख्याएँ 11 से विभाज्य हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"75"},"2":{"en":"86"},"3":{"en":"65"},"4":{"en":"96"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"First multiple above 50: \\(11 \\times 5 = 55\\)<br>Last multiple below 1000: \\(11 \\times 90 = 990\\)<br>Count \\(= 90 - 5 + 1 = \\boxed{86}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 86.</b>","hi":"50 से बड़ा पहला गुणज: \\(11 \\times 5 = 55\\)<br>1000 से छोटा अंतिम गुणज: \\(11 \\times 90 = 990\\)<br>संख्या \\(= 90 - 5 + 1 = \\boxed{86}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 86 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072647","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"P and Q can complete a work in 10 days and 30 days respectively. P starts the work and they work on alternate days. In how many days will the work be completed? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"P और Q एक कार्य को क्रमशः 10 दिनों और 30 दिनों में पूरा कर सकते हैं। P कार्य शुरू करता है और वे एकांतर दिनों में कार्य करते हैं। कार्य कितने दिनों में पूरा होगा? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7 days","hi":"7 दिन"},"2":{"en":"\\(11\\frac{2}{3}\\) days","hi":"\\(11\\frac{2}{3}\\) दिन"},"3":{"en":"\\(14\\frac{2}{3}\\) days","hi":"\\(14\\frac{2}{3}\\) दिन"},"4":{"en":"15 days","hi":"15 दिन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"P's one-day work \\(= \\frac{1}{10}\\), Q's \\(= \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>Work in a 2-day cycle \\(= \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{30} = \\frac{4}{30} = \\frac{2}{15}\\)<br>In 7 cycles (14 days) \\(= \\frac{14}{15}\\), remaining \\(\\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>Day 15 is P's turn, who does \\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) per day, so he needs \\(\\frac{1/15}{1/10} = \\frac{2}{3}\\) day<br>Total \\(= 14\\frac{2}{3}\\) days \\(= \\boxed{14\\frac{2}{3}\\ \\text{days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(14\\frac{2}{3}\\) days.</b>","hi":"P का एक-दिन का कार्य \\(= \\frac{1}{10}\\), Q का \\(= \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>2 दिन के चक्र में कार्य \\(= \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{30} = \\frac{4}{30} = \\frac{2}{15}\\)<br>7 चक्रों (14 दिन) में \\(= \\frac{14}{15}\\), शेष \\(\\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>15वाँ दिन P की बारी है, जो \\(\\frac{1}{10}\\) प्रतिदिन करता है, अतः उसे \\(\\frac{1/15}{1/10} = \\frac{2}{3}\\) दिन लगेगा<br>कुल \\(= 14\\frac{2}{3}\\) दिन \\(= \\boxed{14\\frac{2}{3}\\ \\text{दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(14\\frac{2}{3}\\) दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072648","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"Two ships are sailing on the same side of a lighthouse. The angles of elevation of the top of the lighthouse from them are 30° and 45°. The lighthouse is 60 m high. Find the approximate distance between the ships. (Take √3 = 1.732) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"दो जहाज़ एक ही दिशा में लाइटहाउस के एक ओर जा रहे हैं। उनसे लाइटहाउस के शिखर के उन्नयन कोण 30° और 45° हैं। लाइटहाउस 60 m ऊँचा है। जहाज़ों के बीच की अनुमानित दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। (√3 = 1.732 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"45 m"},"2":{"en":"44 m"},"3":{"en":"41 m"},"4":{"en":"39 m"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Distance of the nearer ship \\(= \\frac{60}{\\tan 45°} = 60\\) m<br>Distance of the farther ship \\(= \\frac{60}{\\tan 30°} = 60\\sqrt{3} = 103.92\\) m<br>Distance between them \\(= 103.92 - 60 = 43.92 \\approx \\boxed{44\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 44 m.</b>","hi":"निकट के जहाज़ की दूरी \\(= \\frac{60}{\\tan 45°} = 60\\) m<br>दूर के जहाज़ की दूरी \\(= \\frac{60}{\\tan 30°} = 60\\sqrt{3} = 103.92\\) m<br>उनके बीच की दूरी \\(= 103.92 - 60 = 43.92 \\approx \\boxed{44\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 44 m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072649","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{3}\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{\\text{cosec}^2\\theta + \\sec^2\\theta}{\\text{cosec}^2\\theta - \\sec^2\\theta}\\). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{3}\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{\\text{cosec}^2\\theta + \\sec^2\\theta}{\\text{cosec}^2\\theta - \\sec^2\\theta}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{3}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"−2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\text{cosec}^2\\theta = \\frac{4}{3}\\), \\(\\sec^2\\theta = 4\\)<br>\\(\\frac{4/3 + 4}{4/3 - 4} = \\frac{16/3}{-8/3} = \\boxed{-2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): −2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan\\theta = \\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow \\sin\\theta = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}, \\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\text{cosec}^2\\theta = \\frac{4}{3}\\), \\(\\sec^2\\theta = 4\\)<br>\\(\\frac{4/3 + 4}{4/3 - 4} = \\frac{16/3}{-8/3} = \\boxed{-2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): −2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072650","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{2} = 1.414\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{2} = 1.414\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.346"},"2":{"en":"4.786"},"3":{"en":"6.242"},"4":{"en":"8.654"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} + 2 = 3\\sqrt{2} + 2\\)<br>\\(= 3(1.414) + 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6.242}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 6.242.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{6 + 2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}} + 2 = 3\\sqrt{2} + 2\\)<br>\\(= 3(1.414) + 2\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{6.242}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 6.242 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072651","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A circle has a diameter of 20 cm. Two equal chords AB and CD are parallel. BC is a diameter of the circle. If chord AB is 6 cm away from the centre, find the length of chord CD (in cm). [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त का व्यास 20 cm है। दो बराबर जीवाएँ AB और CD समांतर हैं। BC वृत्त का व्यास है। यदि जीवा AB केंद्र से 6 cm दूर है, तो जीवा CD की लंबाई (cm में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"16 cm"},"3":{"en":"24 cm"},"4":{"en":"32 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Radius \\(= 10\\) cm; half of AB \\(= \\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8\\) cm, so AB \\(= 16\\) cm<br>The equal chords are equidistant from the centre, so CD is also 6 cm from the centre<br>Hence CD is also \\(2 \\times 8 = \\boxed{16\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16 cm.</b>","hi":"त्रिज्या \\(= 10\\) cm; AB का आधा \\(= \\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = 8\\) cm, अतः AB \\(= 16\\) cm<br>बराबर जीवाएँ केंद्र से समान दूरी पर होती हैं, अतः CD भी केंद्र से 6 cm दूर है<br>इसलिए CD भी \\(2 \\times 8 = \\boxed{16\\ \\text{cm}}\\) है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072652","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A tangent is drawn to a circle of radius 55 cm at point A. A chord BC is parallel to this tangent. If the perpendicular distance from centre O to chord BC is 33 cm, what is the length of chord BC? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"55 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त पर बिंदु A पर स्पर्श रेखा खींची जाती है। एक जीवा BC इस स्पर्श रेखा के समांतर है। यदि केंद्र O से जीवा BC तक लंबवत दूरी 33 cm है, तो जीवा BC की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"74 cm"},"2":{"en":"85 cm"},"3":{"en":"88 cm"},"4":{"en":"96 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Half chord \\(= \\sqrt{55^2 - 33^2} = \\sqrt{3025 - 1089} = \\sqrt{1936} = 44\\) cm<br>Chord BC \\(= 2 \\times 44 = \\boxed{88\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 88 cm.</b>","hi":"आधी जीवा \\(= \\sqrt{55^2 - 33^2} = \\sqrt{3025 - 1089} = \\sqrt{1936} = 44\\) cm<br>जीवा BC \\(= 2 \\times 44 = \\boxed{88\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 88 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072653","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A sector of a circle has a perimeter of 45 cm and its radius is 12 cm. Find the angle of the sector in radians. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"एक वृत्त के त्रिज्यखंड का परिमाप 45 cm है और उसकी त्रिज्या 12 cm है। त्रिज्यखंड का कोण रेडियन में ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1.75 radians","hi":"1.75 रेडियन"},"2":{"en":"2.54 radians","hi":"2.54 रेडियन"},"3":{"en":"3.65 radians","hi":"3.65 रेडियन"},"4":{"en":"5.78 radians","hi":"5.78 रेडियन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Perimeter \\(= r + r + \\text{arc} = 24 + \\text{arc} = 45 \\Rightarrow \\text{arc} = 21\\) cm<br>\\(\\text{arc} = r\\theta \\Rightarrow \\theta = \\frac{21}{12}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1.75\\ \\text{radians}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1.75 radians.</b>","hi":"परिमाप \\(= r + r + \\text{चाप} = 24 + \\text{चाप} = 45 \\Rightarrow \\text{चाप} = 21\\) cm<br>\\(\\text{चाप} = r\\theta \\Rightarrow \\theta = \\frac{21}{12}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1.75\\ \\text{radians}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1.75 रेडियन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072654","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If the expression 64x² + kxy + 81y² is a perfect square, what are the possible values of k? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"यदि व्यंजक 64x² + kxy + 81y² पूर्ण वर्ग है, तो k के संभावित मान क्या हैं? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"±72"},"2":{"en":"±102"},"3":{"en":"36"},"4":{"en":"±144"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For a perfect square, \\(kxy = \\pm 2\\sqrt{64x^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{81y^2}\\)<br>\\(k = \\pm 2 \\times 8 \\times 9\\)<br>\\(k = \\boxed{\\pm 144}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ±144.</b>","hi":"पूर्ण वर्ग के लिए \\(kxy = \\pm 2\\sqrt{64x^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{81y^2}\\)<br>\\(k = \\pm 2 \\times 8 \\times 9\\)<br>\\(k = \\boxed{\\pm 144}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ±144 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072655","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two identical circles, each of radius r, are placed such that the distance between their centers is d. What is the ratio of the length of their direct common tangent segment to the distance between their centers? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]","hi":"r त्रिज्या वाले दो समान वृत्त इस प्रकार रखे गए हैं कि उनके केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी d है। उनकी सीधी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा खंड की लंबाई का केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी से अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 : 1"},"2":{"en":"r : d"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{\\frac{d^2}{4r^2}} : d\\)"},"4":{"en":"2d : r"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Direct common tangent \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r - r)^2} = \\sqrt{d^2} = d\\)<br>Ratio \\(= d : d\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1 : 1.</b>","hi":"सीधी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (r - r)^2} = \\sqrt{d^2} = d\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= d : d\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1 : 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072656","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Obesity, a complex and multifactorial health issue, has reached epidemic proportions globally. Characterized by an excessive accumulation of body fat, obesity is far more than a mere aesthetic concern—it significantly elevates the risk of numerous chronic diseases, including type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disorders, and certain cancers. While sedentary lifestyles and high-calorie diets are commonly cited as primary causes, the reality is nuanced. Genetic predispositions, environmental factors, psychological conditions, and socio-economic status collectively influence an individual’s propensity to gain weight.<br><br>Moreover, modern urban environments often exacerbate the issue, offering limited access to nutritious food options while promoting a culture of convenience and inactivity. Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable, setting the stage for lifelong health struggles. Although public health campaigns have emphasized diet and exercise, long-term success remains elusive for many individuals. This suggests that sustainable solutions must transcend personal responsibility and address systemic barriers.<br><br>Medical interventions, such as pharmacotherapy and bariatric surgery, have offered relief for some, but they are not without risks and are often financially inaccessible. Ultimately, combating obesity requires a multifaceted strategy that integrates education, urban planning, policy reform, and community-based initiatives. Without a comprehensive and empathetic approach, the human and economic costs of the obesity epidemic will continue to escalate, undermining global health systems and shortening life expectancy for millions.<br><br><br><b>Identify the correct tense used in the sentence:</b><br><br>\"Medical interventions, such as pharmacotherapy and bariatric surgery, have offered relief for some, but they are not without risks.\" [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Past Perfect"},"2":{"en":"Present perfect"},"3":{"en":"Simple Past"},"4":{"en":"Present Continuous"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Medical interventions … have offered relief for some…\"</i><br>The main verb is 'have offered' = have + V3, which is the present perfect tense.<br>Past Perfect needs 'had + V3'.<br>Simple Past would be 'offered' alone.<br>Present Continuous needs 'am/is/are + V-ing'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Present perfect.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072657","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Obesity, a complex and multifactorial health issue, has reached epidemic proportions globally. Characterized by an excessive accumulation of body fat, obesity is far more than a mere aesthetic concern—it significantly elevates the risk of numerous chronic diseases, including type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disorders, and certain cancers. While sedentary lifestyles and high-calorie diets are commonly cited as primary causes, the reality is nuanced. Genetic predispositions, environmental factors, psychological conditions, and socio-economic status collectively influence an individual’s propensity to gain weight.<br><br>Moreover, modern urban environments often exacerbate the issue, offering limited access to nutritious food options while promoting a culture of convenience and inactivity. Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable, setting the stage for lifelong health struggles. Although public health campaigns have emphasized diet and exercise, long-term success remains elusive for many individuals. This suggests that sustainable solutions must transcend personal responsibility and address systemic barriers.<br><br>Medical interventions, such as pharmacotherapy and bariatric surgery, have offered relief for some, but they are not without risks and are often financially inaccessible. Ultimately, combating obesity requires a multifaceted strategy that integrates education, urban planning, policy reform, and community-based initiatives. Without a comprehensive and empathetic approach, the human and economic costs of the obesity epidemic will continue to escalate, undermining global health systems and shortening life expectancy for millions.<br><br><br><b>Which voice is used in the sentence:</b><br><br>\"Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable.\" [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Active Voice"},"2":{"en":"Passive Voice"},"3":{"en":"Causative Voice"},"4":{"en":"Interrogative Voice"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable.\"</i><br>'are' is a linking verb followed by the adjective 'vulnerable'; there is no 'be + V3' structure, so the sentence is in the active voice.<br>Passive Voice – needs be + V3 (e.g. 'are affected')<br>Causative Voice – needs have/get + object + V3<br>Interrogative – this is a form of sentence (question), not a voice; the sentence is a statement<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Active Voice.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072658","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Obesity, a complex and multifactorial health issue, has reached epidemic proportions globally. Characterized by an excessive accumulation of body fat, obesity is far more than a mere aesthetic concern—it significantly elevates the risk of numerous chronic diseases, including type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disorders, and certain cancers. While sedentary lifestyles and high-calorie diets are commonly cited as primary causes, the reality is nuanced. Genetic predispositions, environmental factors, psychological conditions, and socio-economic status collectively influence an individual’s propensity to gain weight.<br><br>Moreover, modern urban environments often exacerbate the issue, offering limited access to nutritious food options while promoting a culture of convenience and inactivity. Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable, setting the stage for lifelong health struggles. Although public health campaigns have emphasized diet and exercise, long-term success remains elusive for many individuals. This suggests that sustainable solutions must transcend personal responsibility and address systemic barriers.<br><br>Medical interventions, such as pharmacotherapy and bariatric surgery, have offered relief for some, but they are not without risks and are often financially inaccessible. Ultimately, combating obesity requires a multifaceted strategy that integrates education, urban planning, policy reform, and community-based initiatives. Without a comprehensive and empathetic approach, the human and economic costs of the obesity epidemic will continue to escalate, undermining global health systems and shortening life expectancy for millions.<br><br><br>What is the closest meaning of <b>\"propensity\"</b> as used in the passage? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hesitation"},"2":{"en":"Tendency"},"3":{"en":"Resistance"},"4":{"en":"Disinterest"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…collectively influence an individual’s propensity to gain weight.\"</i><br><b>Propensity (प्रवृत्ति, झुकाव)</b> = a natural tendency to behave in a certain way.<br><b>Tendency (प्रवृत्ति)</b> = inclination ✔<br><b>Hesitation (झिझक)</b> = pausing from uncertainty<br><b>Resistance (प्रतिरोध)</b> = opposing something – opposite sense<br><b>Disinterest (अरुचि)</b> = lack of interest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Tendency.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072659","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Obesity, a complex and multifactorial health issue, has reached epidemic proportions globally. Characterized by an excessive accumulation of body fat, obesity is far more than a mere aesthetic concern—it significantly elevates the risk of numerous chronic diseases, including type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disorders, and certain cancers. While sedentary lifestyles and high-calorie diets are commonly cited as primary causes, the reality is nuanced. Genetic predispositions, environmental factors, psychological conditions, and socio-economic status collectively influence an individual’s propensity to gain weight.<br><br>Moreover, modern urban environments often exacerbate the issue, offering limited access to nutritious food options while promoting a culture of convenience and inactivity. Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable, setting the stage for lifelong health struggles. Although public health campaigns have emphasized diet and exercise, long-term success remains elusive for many individuals. This suggests that sustainable solutions must transcend personal responsibility and address systemic barriers.<br><br>Medical interventions, such as pharmacotherapy and bariatric surgery, have offered relief for some, but they are not without risks and are often financially inaccessible. Ultimately, combating obesity requires a multifaceted strategy that integrates education, urban planning, policy reform, and community-based initiatives. Without a comprehensive and empathetic approach, the human and economic costs of the obesity epidemic will continue to escalate, undermining global health systems and shortening life expectancy for millions.<br><br><br>Choose the synonym of <b>\"exacerbate\"</b> from the options below. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Worsen"},"2":{"en":"Alleviate"},"3":{"en":"Initiate"},"4":{"en":"Neutralize"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Moreover, modern urban environments often exacerbate the issue…\"</i><br><b>Exacerbate (बढ़ाना, और बिगाड़ना)</b> = to make a problem worse.<br><b>Worsen (बदतर करना)</b> ✔<br><b>Alleviate (कम करना)</b> = to make less severe – antonym<br><b>Initiate (आरंभ करना)</b> = to begin – the issue already exists<br><b>Neutralize (निष्प्रभावी करना)</b> = to cancel the effect – antonym<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Worsen.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072660","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Obesity, a complex and multifactorial health issue, has reached epidemic proportions globally. Characterized by an excessive accumulation of body fat, obesity is far more than a mere aesthetic concern—it significantly elevates the risk of numerous chronic diseases, including type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disorders, and certain cancers. While sedentary lifestyles and high-calorie diets are commonly cited as primary causes, the reality is nuanced. Genetic predispositions, environmental factors, psychological conditions, and socio-economic status collectively influence an individual’s propensity to gain weight.<br><br>Moreover, modern urban environments often exacerbate the issue, offering limited access to nutritious food options while promoting a culture of convenience and inactivity. Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable, setting the stage for lifelong health struggles. Although public health campaigns have emphasized diet and exercise, long-term success remains elusive for many individuals. This suggests that sustainable solutions must transcend personal responsibility and address systemic barriers.<br><br>Medical interventions, such as pharmacotherapy and bariatric surgery, have offered relief for some, but they are not without risks and are often financially inaccessible. Ultimately, combating obesity requires a multifaceted strategy that integrates education, urban planning, policy reform, and community-based initiatives. Without a comprehensive and empathetic approach, the human and economic costs of the obesity epidemic will continue to escalate, undermining global health systems and shortening life expectancy for millions.<br><br><br>According to the passage, why are children particularly vulnerable to obesity? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Because children naturally prefer high-calorie foods."},"2":{"en":"Because urban environments often promote unhealthy habits early in life."},"3":{"en":"Because genetic factors are stronger in childhood than adulthood."},"4":{"en":"Because schools are solely responsible for promoting nutrition."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…modern urban environments … offering limited access to nutritious food options while promoting a culture of convenience and inactivity. Children growing up in such settings are particularly vulnerable…\"</i><br>'Such settings' refers to urban environments that promote poor eating and inactivity, so children pick up unhealthy habits early.<br>Option 1 – a natural preference is not mentioned<br>Option 3 – genetics are mentioned, but not as stronger in childhood<br>Option 4 – schools are not mentioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Because urban environments often promote unhealthy habits early in life.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072661","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Complete the collocation by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br><br>Despite the groundbreaking nature of their discovery, the research team decided ________ all the experimental data had been thoroughly verified and peer-reviewed. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"break even"},"2":{"en":"to keep it under wraps"},"3":{"en":"above my hand"},"4":{"en":"slipped my mind"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Keep something under wraps (गुप्त रखना) = to keep something secret.</b><br>A team with a major discovery keeps it secret until the data is verified, so 'decided to keep it under wraps' fits; 'decided' also needs a to-infinitive.<br>Example: The company kept its new model under wraps until the launch.<br><b>Break even (न लाभ न हानि)</b> = neither gain nor lose money<br><b>Above my hand</b> – not an English idiom<br><b>Slipped my mind (भूल जाना)</b> = forgot – does not fit 'decided'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): to keep it under wraps.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072662","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>In a landmark moment for space exploration,<br>P. offering unprecedented insights into planetary formation and the conditions necessary for life,<br>Q. raising the possibility of habitable worlds beyond our solar system,<br>R. the James Webb Space Telescope detected the presence of complex organic molecules in the atmosphere of an exoplanet,<br>S. while astronomers cautioned that further studies were required to confirm the findings [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QSRP"},"2":{"en":"QPRS"},"3":{"en":"RPQS"},"4":{"en":"SRPQ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPQS</b><br><b>R</b> gives the main clause with subject and verb: 'the James Webb Space Telescope detected… molecules…'.<br><b>P</b> 'offering unprecedented insights…' describes what the detection gave.<br><b>Q</b> 'raising the possibility of habitable worlds…' adds a further effect.<br><b>S</b> 'while astronomers cautioned…' ends with the note of caution.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): RPQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072663","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with an appropriate phrasal verb.<br><br>Despite repeated warnings, he ______ risky investments and lost everything. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"plowed into"},"2":{"en":"plowed over"},"3":{"en":"plowed away"},"4":{"en":"plowed through"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Plow (plough) into (बिना सोचे पैसा लगाना) = to invest a large amount of money in something.</b><br>Correct sentence: Despite repeated warnings, he <b>plowed into</b> risky investments and lost everything.<br><b>Plow over</b> = to run over or knock down<br><b>Plow away</b> = to keep working hard at something<br><b>Plow through (कठिनाई से पूरा करना)</b> = to finish something long or difficult, e.g. a book<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): plowed into.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072664","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>The escalating climate crisis<br>P. with rising sea levels and extreme weather patterns<br>Q. has intensified global efforts towards mitigation,<br>R. urging industries to adopt sustainable practices<br>S. while reinforcing commitments to international climate accords [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPRS"},"2":{"en":"SRPQ"},"3":{"en":"SPRQ"},"4":{"en":"RSPQ"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPRS</b><br><b>Q</b> gives the verb for the subject 'The escalating climate crisis': 'has intensified global efforts towards mitigation,'.<br><b>P</b> 'with rising sea levels and extreme weather patterns' explains the crisis.<br><b>R</b> 'urging industries to adopt sustainable practices' shows the result.<br><b>S</b> 'while reinforcing commitments…' adds the second result and ends the sentence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QPRS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072665","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>The parents are <b>in high spirits</b> as their son has got a decent job. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Very happy"},"2":{"en":"Feeling dizzy"},"3":{"en":"Extremely angry"},"4":{"en":"In a confused state"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>In high spirits (बहुत प्रसन्न) = very cheerful and happy.</b><br>The son has got a good job, so the parents are delighted.<br>Example: The team was in high spirits after the victory.<br>Feeling dizzy (चक्कर आना) – unrelated<br>Extremely angry (बहुत क्रोधित) – opposite mood<br>In a confused state (उलझन में) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Very happy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072666","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>The committee decided their decision. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"committee"},"2":{"en":"decided"},"3":{"en":"their"},"4":{"en":"decision"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'decision' collocates with 'make', 'take' or 'announce', not 'decide' (decide a decision is redundant).</b><br>The error is the verb 'decided'.<br>Correct sentence: The committee <b>made / announced</b> their decision.<br>'committee' – correct subject<br>'their' – a collective noun acting as individuals may take 'their'<br>'decision' – correct object<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): decided.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072667","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following options is NOT one of the meanings of the homonym 'panel'? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A group of people chosen to give advice or judgement"},"2":{"en":"A flat, usually rectangular piece forming part of a surface or structure"},"3":{"en":"A touchscreen interface or display area"},"4":{"en":"A legal fee charged per hearing"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Panel (पैनल) – a homonym with several meanings.</b><br>A group of experts or judges: 'a panel of judges' – valid<br>A flat piece forming part of a door, wall or structure: 'a wooden panel' – valid<br>A board or screen with controls or displays: 'a control panel, touch panel' – valid<br>'A legal fee charged per hearing' is not a meaning of 'panel'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): A legal fee charged per hearing.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072668","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>\"I don’t believe Tara really hurt herself when she fell. I think she’s crying <b>crocodile tears</b> just to get attention.\" [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Genuine sadness and emotional pain"},"2":{"en":"Tears caused by a physical injury"},"3":{"en":"Insincere or fake tears meant to fool others"},"4":{"en":"A loud and dramatic cry of joy"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Crocodile tears (घड़ियाली आँसू) = false sorrow shown to deceive others.</b><br>The speaker believes Tara is not hurt and is crying only for attention.<br>Example: The cheat shed crocodile tears before the judge.<br>Genuine sadness (सच्चा दुख) – opposite meaning<br>Tears caused by injury (चोट के आँसू) – the speaker says she is not hurt<br>Cry of joy (खुशी के आँसू) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Insincere or fake tears meant to fool others.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072669","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>MALEDICTION</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prayer"},"2":{"en":"Hope"},"3":{"en":"Blessing"},"4":{"en":"Curse"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Malediction (श्राप, अभिशाप) = a curse; words wishing evil on someone.</b><br><b>Curse (श्राप)</b> = a wish that harm will come to someone ✔<br><b>Prayer (प्रार्थना)</b> = a request to God<br><b>Hope (आशा)</b> = expectation of good<br><b>Blessing (आशीर्वाद)</b> = a wish for good – antonym<br>More synonyms: imprecation, anathema, execration.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Curse.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072670","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word.<b>Prudent</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reckless"},"2":{"en":"Wise"},"3":{"en":"Thoughtful"},"4":{"en":"Careful"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Prudent (विवेकी, समझदार) = acting with care and thought for the future.</b><br><b>Reckless (लापरवाह)</b> = acting without thinking of danger ✔<br><b>Wise (बुद्धिमान)</b> – synonym<br><b>Thoughtful (विचारशील)</b> – synonym<br><b>Careful (सावधान)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: rash, imprudent, careless.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Reckless.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072671","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>ABSTRUSE</b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Evident"},"2":{"en":"Spartan"},"3":{"en":"Obscure"},"4":{"en":"Common"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Abstruse (दुर्बोध) = difficult to understand.</b><br><b>Obscure (अस्पष्ट)</b> = not clear or easily understood ✔<br><b>Evident (स्पष्ट)</b> = clearly seen – antonym<br><b>Spartan (सादा, कठोर)</b> = simple and strict, without comfort<br><b>Common (सामान्य)</b> = ordinary<br>More synonyms: recondite, esoteric, arcane.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Obscure.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072672","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which is the <b>correct spelling</b> of a word meaning 'prevent from happening'? [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Avert"},"2":{"en":"Avart"},"3":{"en":"Avirrt"},"4":{"en":"Avurt"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Avert (टालना, रोकना) = to prevent something bad from happening.</b><br>Spelling: a-v-<b>e</b>-r-t.<br><b>Avart</b> – 'a' in place of 'e'<br><b>Avirrt</b> – 'i' in place of 'e' and a double 'r'<br><b>Avurt</b> – 'u' in place of 'e'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Avert.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072673","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the <b>misspelt</b> word. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Belligerent"},"2":{"en":"Beligerent"},"3":{"en":"Ineffable"},"4":{"en":"Inscrutable"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Belligerent (युद्धप्रिय, झगड़ालू) = hostile and aggressive.</b><br><b>Beligerent</b> is misspelt – it needs a double 'l' (be-<b>ll</b>-igerent).<br><b>Belligerent</b> – correct<br><b>Ineffable (अवर्णनीय)</b> = too great to be described in words – correct<br><b>Inscrutable (रहस्यमय)</b> = impossible to understand – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Beligerent.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072674","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitution</b> for: ‘The act of stealing from shops’. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Robbery"},"2":{"en":"Looting"},"3":{"en":"Burglary"},"4":{"en":"Shoplifting"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Shoplifting (दुकान से चोरी) = stealing goods from a shop while pretending to be a customer.</b><br><b>Robbery (डकैती)</b> = stealing from a person using force or threat<br><b>Looting (लूटपाट)</b> = stealing during riots, war or disorder<br><b>Burglary (सेंधमारी)</b> = breaking into a building to steal<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Shoplifting.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072675","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>They have denied the allegations. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The allegations are denied."},"2":{"en":"The allegations were denied."},"3":{"en":"The allegations have been denied."},"4":{"en":"The allegations had been denied."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect active (have + V3) → passive: have/has + been + V3.</b><br>'the allegations' becomes the subject; 'by them' is dropped.<br>Passive: The allegations <b>have been denied</b>.<br>Option 1 – simple present passive<br>Option 2 – simple past passive<br>Option 4 – past perfect passive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): The allegations have been denied.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072676","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>My brother <b><i>is good in cricket.</i></b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"good to cricket"},"2":{"en":"best in cricket"},"3":{"en":"is good at cricket"},"4":{"en":"well in cricket"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'good at' is used for skill in an activity or subject.</b><br>'good in' is wrong for a skill such as a sport.<br>Correct sentence: My brother <b>is good at</b> cricket.<br>good to cricket – wrong preposition and verb 'is' missing<br>best in cricket – verb missing and superlative not needed<br>well in cricket – 'well' is an adverb; verb missing<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): is good at cricket.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072677","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>They have been working on this project <b><i>since four months.</i></b> [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"from four months"},"2":{"en":"for past four months"},"3":{"en":"since last four months"},"4":{"en":"for four months"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'for' is used with a period of time; 'since' with a point of time.</b><br>'four months' is a period, so 'for' is required with the present perfect continuous.<br>Correct sentence: They have been working on this project <b>for four months</b>.<br>from four months – 'from' needs a starting point<br>for past four months – article 'the' missing ('for the past four months')<br>since last four months – 'since' cannot take a period<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): for four months.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072678","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences to form a meaningful passage:</b><br>1. Ancient Greek democracy laid the foundation for civic participation.2. Citizens debated laws in public assemblies.3. This model influenced later republics worldwide.4. However, rights were limited to free adult males. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-4-2-3"},"2":{"en":"2-1-3-4"},"3":{"en":"1-2-4-3"},"4":{"en":"4-1-2-3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 1-2-4-3</b><br><b>1</b> introduces the topic: Greek democracy laid the foundation for civic participation.<br><b>2</b> explains how citizens took part: debating laws in assemblies.<br><b>4</b> 'However' adds the limitation of this participation.<br><b>3</b> 'This model' sums up and concludes with its later influence.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1-2-4-3.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072679","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Rearrange the following sentences to form a coherent paragraph:</b><br>1. This process ensures that the food we eat is safe and does not contain harmful bacteria or other contaminants.2. Food processing is a series of methods used to transform raw ingredients into consumable products.3. These methods can range from simple actions like cutting and grinding to more complex procedures such as pasteurization and fermentation.4. Furthermore, it also helps to preserve food, extend its shelf life, and enhance its nutritional value. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2, 3, 1, 4"},"2":{"en":"1, 2, 3, 4"},"3":{"en":"3, 1, 4, 2"},"4":{"en":"4, 2, 1, 3"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2, 3, 1, 4</b><br><b>2</b> defines food processing – the opening sentence.<br><b>3</b> 'These methods' refers to the 'series of methods' in 2.<br><b>1</b> 'This process' gives the first benefit: safe food.<br><b>4</b> 'Furthermore, it also' adds further benefits and closes the paragraph.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2, 3, 1, 4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072680","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.</b><br><br>The new law had a <b><u>pernicious</u></b> effect on the local economy. [SSC CGL 01/10/26 Shift 1]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Beneficial"},"2":{"en":"Harmful"},"3":{"en":"Damaging"},"4":{"en":"Deleterious"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Pernicious (अत्यंत हानिकारक) = having a harmful effect, especially gradually.</b><br><b>Beneficial (लाभदायक)</b> = having a good effect ✔<br><b>Harmful (हानिकारक)</b> – synonym<br><b>Damaging (नुकसानदायक)</b> – synonym<br><b>Deleterious (हानिकारक)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: advantageous, wholesome, salutary.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Beneficial.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};